\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ \uc2 Brazil's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Believes Real Weakening Too Fast - Source\b0\par\par\uc2 891 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2012\par 20:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 6 Dec 2012 14:27 EDT *DJ  \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thinks \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Movement Is 'Artificial' - Source\par \par \uc2 6 Dec 2012 14:27 EDT *DJ  \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : Exchange Rate Doesn't Reflect Fundamentals -Source\par \par \uc2 6 Dec 2012 14:27 EDT *DJ  \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Has No Floor or Ceiling for Real - Source\par \par \uc2 6 Dec 2012 14:42 EDT DJ  \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thinks Real Weakening Too Fast - Source\par \par \uc2 --Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes market has made an incorrect assessment of government policy, a person familiar with the policy says\par \par \uc2 --That impression in the market led to an "artificial depreciation" of the real, according to the person\par \par \uc2 --Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes the real doesn't reflect economic fundamentals, the person says \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Luciana Magalhaes \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  believes there has been "an artificial depreciation" of the Brazilian real as the market is working on an erroneous view of government policy, according to a person familiar with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's thinking.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The market is working based on conjectures, on a belief that the government wants a weaker real," said the person, who asked not to be identified. "But there's no band. There's no roof and no floor. The market determines the exchange rate."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Current exchange rate levels versus the dollar don't reflect the fundamentals of the Brazilian economy, which, in spite of the weak performance, is "growing more" than other economies, said the person.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While debate persists about the real's fair value--it's lost around 10% against the dollar so far this year, but many economists still see it as overvalued --there is also a general perception that it has shed weight too fast against the dollar in recent sessions.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 There have been a series of press reports citing people close to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that have helped strengthen the Brazilian real over the last two days. The real traded at BRL2.0782 on Thursday afternoon, stronger than Wednesday's close of BRL2.0978, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The signals appear to have arrested a concerted effort by some in the market to test weaker levels for the Brazilian real. The real weakened to 2.1359 in intraday trading on Nov. 30.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Last week, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  touched BRL2.0978 per dollar during intraday trading, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stepped in several times to strengthen the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Tuesday and Wednesday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also relaxed some restrictions on capital inflows that had been introduced earlier this year to prevent an overappreciation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Although officially these were more aimed at specific issues in lending markets, market players saw the move as clearly directed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We had a problem of dollar liquidity and the government acted to solve that", said Sidnei Nehme, executive director at Brazilian brokerage NGO. Next year could be challenging for the real, as the government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , combined with historic low interest rates, has made \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  less attractive to overseas investors, Mr. Nehme said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The efforts to avoid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakness come just as some in the rates market raised questions about monetary policy next year. There's a growing perception that the central won't raise rates in 2013 and may even start cutting them again to speed up the pace of recovery.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 After timid 2.7% growth in 2011, the Brazilian economy is expected to grow just 1% or even less in 2012, despite a series of measures taken in an effort to spur growth. The government has often expressed concern that a strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hinders the competitiveness of Brazilian exporters.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is also constrained from cutting interest rates by above-target inflation, which is running around 5.6%. That's more than a full point higher than its 4.5% target, though still within the 6.5% upper limit of its tolerance band.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier Thursday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reaffirmed its commitment to the interest rate stability for a "sufficiently prolonged period," in the minutes of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's monetary policy meeting from Nov. 27 and 28.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the comments from the person familiar with the bank's consideration could once again raise tensions in Brasilia.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The bigger question is whether this new 'strong BRL' policy signals, as some investors now believe, a change in the relative power between the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  over management of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," wrote Tony Volpon, a strategist at Nomura Securities in New York, suggesting the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may have recovered stewardship of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, there's no real contradiction between taking the real lower to help industry and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to moderate the recent sudden depreciation, Mr. Volpon said. The process has to be managed to minimize damage to companies from a stronger \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or inflation from a weaker real.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "But there is no doubt, given the dismal growth in Brazil, that a weaker real is what the government desires," he said. "We still believe that it will settle at a 2.08-2.12 level once the high levels of noise and uncertainty around the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hopefully fade."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Luciana Magalhaes at luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 06, 2012 14:42 ET (19:42 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020121206e8c6005bw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\