\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  GLOBAL CALL: Our Take on the Day's Big  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  News\b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Dezember 2012\par 13:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Global Call covers the main talking points from a news meeting involving DJ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trader editors in New York, London and Singapore, as well as other \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  hot spots when warranted.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     By Brian Baskin \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1. It's official: Nothing can kill the Australian dollar. The \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\uc2  cut interest rates to 3%, the lowest since September 2009--and the Aussie rose. Traders say the gains came as the RBA's statement hinted there won't be any further cuts for a while, though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wasn't scheduled to meet again until February anyway. And the bank was clear on a few points that should be negative for the Aussie, including that the "peak in resource investment is approaching." Still, foreign investors, central banks and sovereign wealth funds continue to flock to triple-A rated, relatively high-yielding Australian bonds. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades at $1.0444, from $1.0421 before the announcement.\par \par \uc2 2. The Swiss franc weakened to an 11-week low of 1.2145 against the euro, extending a slide that began Monday after \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  imposed negative interest rates on deposits in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Tuesday's drop followed rumors that the bank's measures would be more punitive than expected, or that other major banks were about to announce similar plans, neither of which bore out. But those were just the trigger--fact is, with virtually every euro-zone stress indicator nearing precrisis lows, investors don't feel as great a need to hold safe havens like the franc. Tellingly, the other recent time the franc's backed off the 1.20 floor enforced by the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  was in early September, when the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  outlined its bond-buying plan.\par \par \uc2 3. Speaking of those stress indicators: Italian 10-year bond yields fell to a two-year low, trading at about 4.43%. The euro itself hit a six-week high of $1.3077. In both cases, gains were slim.\par \par \uc2 4. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the real for a third consecutive trading day, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains above 2.10 to the dollar. While the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's made a show of support, it hasn't quieted the debate in the market over whether policy makers' true intent is to gradually guide the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a slightly weaker level to help Brazil's struggling economy.\par \par \uc2 5. South Korea and China tweaked a $59 billion bilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap arrangement to make it more attractive to businesses, which so far have yet to use it. Both countries want their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be more easily used outside their borders.\par \par \uc2 6. The U.K. construction purchasing managers index showed the sector going back into contraction in November with a reading of 49.3. Sterling was largely unaffected, as markets wait for Chancellor of the Exchequer \uc2 George Osborne\uc2 's autumn statement on the economy.\par \par \uc2 7. Hong Kong sold HK$3.875 billion ($500 million) to keep the Hong Kong dollar in its target range against the dollar. The HK dollar is in demand and has traded on the high end of its band for nearly two months.\par \par \uc2 (Brian Baskin is assistant managing editor for the Americas at DJ \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  Trader, a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  news service jointly produced by Dow Jones Newswires and The Wall Street Journal.)\par \par \uc2 Subscribe to WSJ: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2  [ 04-12-12 1215GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121204e8c4000lh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
