\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil intervenes \highlight\uc2  heavily on  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  market, real gains\b0\par\par\uc2 570 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2012\par 18:53\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  calls 2 swap auctions in the morning\par \par \uc2 * Later, bank calls 2 auctions to sell dollars on spot market\par \par \uc2 * Real closes 0.5 pct stronger at 2.119 per dollar\par \par \uc2 (Adds quote from analysts, background)\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Dec 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to halt a sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation and boost dollar liquidity at the end of the year, when greenbacks are traditionally scarce in the country.\par \par \uc2 The series of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which included two \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions in the morning and two dollar auctions on the spot market in the afternoon, caused the real to close only 0.5 percent stronger at 2.1190 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Despite the magnitude of the actions, investors believe the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is only trying to smooth out an expected weakening of the real, which lost 4.7 percent in November, half of that in the last week of the month.\par \par \uc2 Bets on a weaker real greatly increased on Friday after data showed the Brazilian economy grew in the third quarter at half the rate expected by economists, but investors still wonder how much the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will allow the real to slide.\par \par \uc2 "We still don't know how much weaker the government wants the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to be," said Joao Medeiros, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at Pioneer brokerage.\par \par \uc2 The real dropped to 2.1382 per dollar right after the market opened, its weakest level in more than 3-1/2 years, before the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called two consecutive auctions to sell traditional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps - derivative contracts that support the real by emulating the sale of dollars in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 The real erased its losses and jumped as much as 1.6 percent after that initial move, which suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not comfortable with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fast depreciation pace. But gains slowly faded in the afternoon as investors followed bank recommendations to reduce exposure to the real.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  then announced two separate auctions to sell as much as $5 billion on the spot market with the agreement to repurchase the amounts sold in 30 and 61 days, respectively.\par \par \uc2 "Investors are becoming long dollars, I believe that is because they need to hedge their positions. Even after two swap auctions, the market wanted more," said Reginaldo Galhardo, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Treviso brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 It was the first time the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars with repurchase agreements since April 2009 - a strategy it normally uses to provide temporary liquidity to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not say how much it sold in the afternoon auctions, but it signaled there was demand for both. In a statement, the bank said it was setting cutoff prices of 2.12245 reais and 2.1324 reais for each of the auctions, with repurchase dates on January 4 and February 4, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Less than two weeks ago, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  president \uc2 Alexandre Tombini\uc2  warned the bank was ready to protect the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from speculative bouts and provide temporary liquidity to the exchange market at year-end.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Danielle Fonseca in Sao Paulo; Editing by Nick Zieminski and Steve Orlofsky)\par \par \uc2 BRAZIL-\b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCY\b0 \highlight\uc2 /AUCTION (UPDATE 2) | ABN | D | E | RBN | U | M | NAT | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121203e8c30015r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
