\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Potential Negatives Priced In for Brazil's OGX\b0\par\par\uc2 1,405 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Dezember 2012\par 15:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 9:26 EST - The negatives plaguing Brazil oil producer \uc2 OGX Petroleo e Gas\uc2  Participacoes SA (OGXP3.BR, OGXPY) are already priced in, says Espirito Santo Investment Bank. Bank upgrades OGX shares to "buy" and raises price target to BRL7.10 as risks now tilted toward upside. Market outlook for OGX to swing on several catalysts, including third production well at Waimea, commercial gas output at Gaviao Real and new platforms set to arrive late next year, bank says. Recent purchase of stake in offshore block, however, likely means $1B Eike Batista put option now "a necessity," bank says. (jeff.fick@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:23 EST - \uc2 New York Fed\uc2  leader Dudley tells a conference on housing at this bank \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  mortgage buying is working. Agency mortgage-bond-securities rates have declined, and "this is solid evidence that our policy has been, and continues to be, effective -- though it is certainly not all-powerful in current circumstances," he says, in remarks flagging the economy's ongoing weakness. Not much new in speech compared to remarks last week. (Michael.derby@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:09 EST - The CEO carousel in the gold-mining sector stops at one of the industry's heavyweights, with CEO \uc2 Richard O'Brien\uc2  stepping down from Newmont (NEM) on March 1 and leaving the board then, being succeeded by President \uc2 Gary Goldberg\uc2 . The 30-year industry vet joined the company a year ago and was given the president's title in July, making him the obvious internal candidate to follow O'Brien if he were to leave. He became CEO in 2007 as gold prices were continuing their multiyear surge. But shares haven't risen much since, despite the metal's price gains, amid rising mining costs that have heavily pressured the industry the past several years. But at least NEM shares haven't fallen since 2007, like some peers have. They haven't traded premarket since the CEO change was announced. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 9:03 EST - The Markit final reading of November US PMI comes in at 52.8, up from flash 52.4 and final October reading of 51.0. November reading is highest since May. The increase sets up an upside risk to the more widely watched ISM PMI out at 10 am ET. Economists expects that index to fall to 51.0 in November, from 51.7 in October. (kathleen.madigan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:56 EST - \uc2 Dean Foods\uc2  (DF) will ultimately be shell of its former self in short order. The company, which had 3 different segments, spun off the middle-sized one into organic-milk and plant-based-beverage maker WhiteWave (WWAV) in late October. Now, the smallest--cream producer Morningstar--is being sold to Saputo (SAP.T) for $1.45B. That will leave DF as a low-margin maker of dairy products, though a company with notably less debt than it had. DF investors approve, with shares up 5% premarket at $18 after having already jumped 53% this year. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:56 EST - Investors who have steadily added to their USD/JPY longs in recent weeks are taking some profits today on concern that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  "might have limited policy options" to weaken the yen, says Thomas Doyle, a managing director at Faros Trading. Expectations that the BOJ will come under increased pressure to ease monetary policy has driven the yen lower in recent weeks. But the daily correction doesn't likely indicate a turnaround in the broader trend, and Doyle says the pair may ultimately rise to near Y84. The dollar was at Y82.27, from Y82.48 late Friday, according to EBS via CQG. It has risen from its intraday low at Y81.99. (matthew.walter@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:45 EST - USD/CAD hovers just above the 0.99 handle to open this week's trading, moving on the better-than-expected read from China's PMI figures that's pushing most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stronger against USD. Tuesday's BOC rate decision looms over the loonie, even though it's widely expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep its policy rate at 1.00%. Trading is typically cautious ahead of policy dates as even just a tweak to the statement's wording, which is about all anybody can expect at this meeting, can move the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . USD/CAD at 0.9917, down 0.24%, according to CQG. (david.george-cosh@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:37 EST - Some \uc2 Health Management Associates\uc2  (HMA) investors are leaving, feeling the heat as "60 Minutes" last night reported on allegations that doctors faced pressure to admit patients from the emergency room to fill hospital beds. The hospital operator calls the report "inaccurate" while noting data show HMA admission rates are in-line with national norms and consistent over several years. But CRT Capital--which found "troubling admit patterns" in its own analysis and cuts HMA to sell from fair value--sees "significantly greater risk" of a bigger federal investigation and potential settlement fines. "This is as serious an allegation of fraud as we have ever heard," CRT adds. HMA is down 3.4% premarket at $7.68. (jon.kamp@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:33 EST - \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  does a 180 on DELL, going from its sell rating of the past 2 years (the stock slumped 31% during that time) to buy on the PC maker and hiking its price target to $13 from $9 even amid last month's dour quarterly report. "While we remain cautious on PC and server demand trends, we believe many of our long-held secular concerns have become consensus." As such, "sentiment and expectations" could begin to "tilt positively in 2013" while the company's $3/share of cash "provides some downside buffer as it produces opportunity for an LBO or levered recap under the right conditions." DELL climbs 5.4% premarket to $10.16. (andrew.fitzgerald@dowjones.com; @drewfitzgerald)\par \par \uc2 8:18 EST - Safe-haven US government bonds are playing defense as Greek debt rallies after its country's debt-buyback program was announced. As an integral part of its broader debt-reduction efforts, Greece indicated it'd offer at least 30-38% of face value for the bonds that are part of the buyback. So despite some contractionary manufacturing numbers. Peripheral euro-zone spreads are tighter, and as such, Treasurys yields are higher. Benchmark 10-year notes are down 10/32, yielding 1.642%. (cynthia.lin@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:14 EST - \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stifling talk of a new range for real, slapping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  back into recent trading range by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice in the local market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real now trades at BRL2.1052 vs USD, sharply stronger from opening quote of BRL2.1297. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sold $1.09 billion in swaps shortly after open, now plans to sell up to an additional $1 billion in swaps. Auctions are a clear signal to market that bank is maintaining BRL2.10 ceiling of recent BRL2.00-BRL2.10 trading range, traders say. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had sat out late November volatile trade to not affect settlement of futures. (Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 8:14 EST - While admitting Deckers' (DECK) sales and margins should "remain challenged" through 1H, Sterne Agee says they "are likely to improve materially" in the back half of 2013 on improved offerings from the footwear and outdoor-apparel maker. Near-term worries have been a ballast around shares of the UGGs maker the past year, tumbling by 2/3 since Halloween 2011. But they jumped 1/3 last month to $38.29 and Sterne Agee sets a $65 target as it upgrades DECK to buy. The investment bank for the past year has "been hypercritical" of management actions "that we felt put the UGG brand at risk," including raising prices without offering much new and boosting distribution. Sterne Agee thinks officials have begun moving "to revitalize the UGG brand for fall 2013." DECK is up 10% premarket at $42.15. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bradley Davis\f28 \uc2 \f2 , 212 416-2654, bradley.davis@dowjones.com \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326,Patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 12-03-12 0926ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020121203e8c30006o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
