\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Opens Stronger, Investors Wary Of  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 649 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2012\par 13:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil real opens at BRL2.0721/dlr vs. BRL2.0818/dlr Friday\par \par \uc2 --Investors "adjusting" positions after Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  move\par \par \uc2 --Exporters sell dollars, help support real against greenback\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Tom Murphy\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real opened stronger against the U.S. dollar on Monday as exporters sold dollars to the market and investors kept a wary eye on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In early trading, the real was changing hands at BRL2.0721 to the dollar, stronger against the Friday close of BRL2.0818, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Friday was a roller-coaster ride for the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, with the real weakening to nearly BRL2.12 to the dollar in early trading. But the swift weakening of the real brought \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the form of an auction of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts. The real strengthened in the wake of the auction, which effectively added dollar-linked paper to the pool of contracts available in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 "Today [Monday], investors are adjusting their positions in the wake of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Reginaldo Siaca, manager of Sao Paulo's Advanced brokerage. "Of course, there is no formal trading band established by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the market is beginning to perceive an informal band around BRL2.02 to BRL2.12. It was evident Friday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not at all like the idea of having the real trade weaker than BRL2.12."\par \par \uc2 Traders said volatility was likely to be muted Monday, with any abrupt movement in the market meeting with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trading could turn move volatile later in the week in the runup to expiry of monthly \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  futures contracts. The contracts will be closed out based on Friday's average \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate, or Ptax rate.\par \par \uc2 "The Ptax close-out could bring some jockeying between holders of long-dollar positions and short positions," said Mr. Siaca.\par \par \uc2 Traders said overseas factors could have more impact than domestic news in the next few days.\par \par \uc2 "Europe will continue to be a focus," said Mr. Siaca.\par \par \uc2 European finance ministers are due to meet Monday to discuss the next phase of a bailout for debt-strapped Greece. Failure to aid Greece could bring a new round of pessimism about Europe's ability to confront deep debt and growth problems.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold its last monetary policy meeting of the year on Wednesday. However, analysts are virtually unanimous in saying the bank will hold its Selic base interest rate steady at 7.25%. Brazil's government is due to release third-quarter economic growth figures on Friday. Analysts expect a robust rebound from the sluggish growth registered in the first half of the year.\par \par \uc2 December could see more volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Traders noted that multinational companies typically increase their profit and dividend remittances toward the end of the year as they square their books with parent companies. Imports also increase ahead of the Christmas season, another factor that could increase the demand for dollars.\par \par \uc2 Heavy demand for the American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could bring more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in December in the event \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides to hold the line against any depreciation beyond the BRL2.12 level.\par \par \uc2 Swap auctions are likely to be the preferred method for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The auctions effectively dump dollar-linked paper into the futures market. Friday's auction added the equivalent of $1.62 billion. That was enough to offset more than half of the $3.14 billion in so-called reverse-swap contracts that will expire Dec. 3. Traders said it was possible the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will use another swap auction before Dec. 3 to offset the rest of the reverse swaps coming due.\par \par \uc2 -Write to \uc2 Tom Murphy\uc2  at tom.murphy@dowjones.com [ 26-11-12 1219GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121126e8bq000my\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
