\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  weaken on Greece anxiety\b0\par\par\uc2 642 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2012\par 18:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  * Latam \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  weighed down by fears over Greece\par \par \uc2  * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real's losses curbed by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns\par \par \uc2  * Mexican peso down 0.32 pct, Brazilian real flat \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, updates prices)\par \par \uc2  By Natalia Cacioli and Jean Arce\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO/MEXICO CITY, Nov 26 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  edged lower on Monday on uncertainty over Greek aid negotiations, which resulted in a debt-cutting agreement reached too late in the day to boost the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2  The Chilean peso lost 0.6 percent while the Mexican peso  fell 0.32 percent on the Greek uncertainty.\par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real  was mostly flat amid expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakens toward the level of 2.1 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  But most investors were eyeing Brussels, where euro zone finance ministers and the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  finally clinched an agreement on a new debt target for Greece, a significant step toward releasing another tranche of loans to the near-bankrupt economy. \par \par \uc2  Mexico's peso has firmed more than 2 percent from a 2-1/2 month low hit earlier this month, supported by easing concerns about fiscal negotiations in the \uc2 U.S. Congress\uc2  and appetite for the country's higher-yielding debt.\par \par \uc2  But U.S. President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 's rejection on Monday of a Republican suggestion for avoiding the "fiscal cliff" has some analysts far from sanguine on the peso's near-term prospects.\par \par \uc2  "We remain pretty neutral on the (Mexican) peso ... but we still think there is room for disappointment in terms of peso volatility," said Delia Paredes, a strategist at Banorte-IXE in Mexico, citing "signs of disagreement in the U.S." \par \par \uc2  She expects the Mexican peso to trade between 12.87 and 13.10 per dollar this week.\par \par \uc2  The White House on Monday threw cold water on a Republican proposal for solving the so-called "fiscal cliff" by limiting tax deductions and loopholes, instead of allowing taxes to rise for the highest earners in the United States. \par \par \uc2  REAL'S NEW TRADING BAND?\par \par \uc2  The Brazilian real closed nearly flat, weakening only 0.03 percent to 2.0818 per greenback as investors digested conflicting signs from policymakers about the future of the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2  The real on Friday posted its largest single-day gain in nearly three months after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped into the market to halt losses that were partly fueled by comments from Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2 .\par \par \uc2  Speaking to business leaders in Sao Paulo, Mantega said Brazil's exchange rate was at a "reasonable though not totally satisfactory level" to support industry. His remarks drove the real as low as 2.1168 per dollar, its weakest level in 3-1/2 years.\par \par \uc2  The apparent tug of war between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Mantega left investors wondering whether policymakers still uphold an informal trading band of 2.0-2.1 per dollar, where the real has been stuck since early July.\par \par \uc2  "I believe the market is still digesting that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Luiz Fernando Genova, a trader with \uc2 Banco Daycoval\uc2  in Sao Paulo. "We have seen the real weakening lately, but it's still too early to say they will change this band."     \par \par \uc2  Latin America \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 12:53 AM GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %    YTD %\par                                   change   change\par                          Latest           \par Brazil real                2.0818    -0.03   -10.25\par                                           \par Mexico peso               13.0215    -0.32    7.280\par                                           \par Argentina peso*            6.4400    -0.47   -26.55\par                                           \par Chile peso               481.5000    -0.60     7.85\par                                           \par Colombia peso          1,825.0000    -0.07     6.21\par                                           \par Peru sol                   2.5880     0.00     4.21\par                                           \par * Argentine peso's rate between                    \par brokerages                                  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Writing by Walter Brandimarte and Alexandra Alper; Editing by\par Peter Galloway and Lisa Shumaker)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121129e8bq0012v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
