\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Closes Stronger After  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 406 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 2012\par 19:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --The real strengthened to BRL2.0818 to the dollar, from BRL2.0957 Thursday\par \par \uc2 --It had weakened to BRL2.1172 in the late morning\par \par \uc2 --The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held a swap auction to halt the slide\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeffrey T. Lewis \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real closed stronger against the dollar Friday after the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to reverse a rapid weakening of the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0818 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset, after briefly weakening to BRL2.1172 in late morning trading, just before the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  announced a swap auction that halted the slide.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders had already been on the lookout for an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Friday after the real closed Thursday near the BRL2.10 level the bank has defended on other occasions. The real quickly moved past that level in early trading Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been defending a trading band of BRL2.00 to BRL2.10 for months, while at the same time denying that it's doing any such thing.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Just Thursday the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's president, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alexandre Tombini\f28 \uc2 \f2 , told Brazil's congress that "we don't have any formal or informal band for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ."\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets have received what might be conflicting signals from Brazilian officials recently. President Dilma Rousseff suggested in an interview published Tuesday in Valor newspaper that the real was still overvalued at current levels, while earlier Friday Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guido Mantega\f28 \uc2 \f2  said the real is in a "reasonable position," while adding the real's level is "still not totally satisfactory."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Friday's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could indicate the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might not be on board with a weaker real, and has left some traders with doubts about the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It looks like they're not all on the same page at the moment," said Joao Medeiros, a partner at the Pioneer Corretora brokerage in Sao Paulo. "That's making things a bit more complex for us."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The bank might really be moving its unofficial range for the real to BRL2.05-BRL2.15, said analysts Tony Volpon and George Lei at Nomura Securities in New York, because Brazilian authorities are relying on the weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost economic growth despite the potential negative effect on inflation.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Jeffrey T. Lewis at jeffrey.lewis@dowjones.com [ 23-11-12 1823GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121123e8bn000oa\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
