\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Brazil real hovers near 3-1/2-year low; pesos rally\b0\par\par\uc2 586 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2012\par 19:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * U.S. lawmakers signal progress in fiscal negotiations\par \par \uc2 * Chile peso firms by most in nearly 2 months\par \par \uc2 * Brazil real flat, Mexico peso up 0.56 pct\par \par \uc2 (Recasts with closing prices, comment)\par \par \uc2 By Natalia Cacioli\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Nov 19 (Reuters) - Mexico's and Chile's pesos firmed on Monday as signs of progress in U.S. fiscal negotiations boosted riskier assets around the globe, while Brazil's real was little changed as it teetered near a 3-1/2-year low.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real traded flat at 2.0810 per dollar, bidding just stronger from its weakest since May 2009 that it hit on Friday.\par \par \uc2 After trading in a narrow range since July, the real last week saw its steepest weekly slump since early June. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's sharp slump is raising the chances that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, analysts said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has frequently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the real's rise from gaining too much ground and hurting local manufacturers, who face competition from cheaper imports when the real gains.\par \par \uc2 But policymakers are also worried that if the real weakens too much it could drive inflation higher by raising the cost of imports. Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to bolster if the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakens to around 2.10 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy not to compromise inflation," said Reginaldo Galhardo, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at brokerage Treviso.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may act if the dollar get closer to 2.10, but it is more likely to act if there is a sharp movement, rather than defend a particular level," he said.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's stock market will be closed for a holiday on Tuesday, which will limit volumes in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and could exacerbate volatility, traders said.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso firmed 1 percent to bid at 479.80 per dollar in its biggest one-day percentage gain in nearly two months while Mexico's peso climbed 0.56 percent to 13.0575 per dollar in international trading with local markets closed for a holiday.\par \par \uc2 Three sessions of gains after six sessions of losses helped improve a grim technical outlook for Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The cost of dollars in pesos fell back below its 200-day simple moving average on Friday and it moved beneath its 100-day average on Monday.\par \par \uc2 A technical indicator called the MACD showed a cross that could bode for further gains in the peso against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Supporting global markets, leading U.S. lawmakers expressed confidence that they could reach a deal to avert abrupt spending cuts and tax hikes that could plunge the U.S. economy into another recession next year.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that euro zone countries will agree on Tuesday on a plan to fund Greece for at least two years added to market optimism.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2150 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \