\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weakens as U.S., Europe Fiscal Issues Weigh\b0\par\par\uc2 453 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2012\par 19:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil real exits active trading at BRL2.0385 to the dollar vs. BRL2.0325 Wednesday\par \par \uc2 --U.S., European fiscal problems continue to weigh on global investors\par \par \uc2 --Volume on Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market grows heading into year-end\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Tom Murphy\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real weakened against the U.S. dollar for the second straight day Thursday as U.S. and European debt problems once again took center stage.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0385 to the dollar, weaker against the Wednesday close of BRL2.0325, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 In a statement Thursday, the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  said looming U.S. political negotiations over tax and spending policies were already creating "uncertainties" in global financial markets. Newly re-elected President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  must reach agreement with a Republican-controlled House of Representatives on fiscal policies for 2013 by the end of the year or face the risk of a new recession.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the IMF offered little solace on global growth prospects, saying recent projections for 2013 growth by the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  finance ministers may have been overly optimistic.\par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2 , in a news conference, also struck a pessimistic note when commenting on regional growth prospects. He praised Greece's parliament for passing fiscal austerity legislation Wednesday night but said Europe's battle for fiscal equilibrium was far from over.\par \par \uc2 The gloomy statements from the IMF and from Europe's top central banker led to weakness for the euro against the U.S. dollar, with the Brazilian real following suit.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, trading volume began to creep up in the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday. Volume typically rises in the last weeks of the year as importers step up purchases of consumer goods ahead of the Christmas season and multinational companies increase profit remittances.\par \par \uc2 According to traders, demand for dollars has been met so far by heavy inflows of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Brazilian companies placing overseas bonds.\par \par \uc2 "Brazilian companies are taking advantage of robust demand [for bond issues] from investors across the globe," said Leandro Miranda, head of fixed-income investments at Brazil's \uc2 Banco Bradesco\uc2 . Heavy demand has kept interest yields low, whetting the appetite of Brazilian companies for more issues, Mr. Miranda added.\par \par \uc2 Later in the year, demand for dollars from importers and multinational companies could outstrip inflows from bond issues. But, in that case, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market as a seller of dollars, traders said. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls foreign reserves in excess of $370 billion.\par \par \uc2 -Write to \uc2 Tom Murphy\uc2  at tom.murphy@dowjones.com [ 08-11-12 1829GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121108e8b8001d4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
