\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Slightly Stronger on Firm Global Markets\b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 November 2012\par 19:29\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil real exits active trading at BRL2.0318/dlr vs BRL2.0336 Monday\par \par \uc2 --Stronger euro, stocks, commodities prices helped support real\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , foreign investors sidelined ahead of U.S. elections\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   By \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tom Murphy\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real strengthened slightly against the U.S. dollar Tuesday, tracking gains for the euro and higher global stocks and commodities prices.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0318 to the dollar, slightly stronger against the Monday close of BRL2.0336, according to Tullet Prebon via FactSet.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In Europe, stocks and the euro strengthened on improved corporate earnings. A stronger euro helped propel gains for international commodities prices. Higher commodities prices favor Brazilian export revenues.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An overall improved tone in global trading Tuesday came as U.S. voters lined up to choose a president and members of congress. Investors are increasingly hopeful the outcome of the U.S. presidential election will become clear within a few hours of the polls closing. If so, the result will also help clarify U.S. fiscal and monetary policies for the next four years.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But traders in Brazil also noted that while volatility was low Tuesday, so was volume.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Trading is sideways," said Mauricianao Cavalcanti, a trader at Sao Paulo's Ouro Mina brokerage. "All eyes are on the U.S. election." He noted that international investors and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were essentially sidelined Tuesday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the longer term, however, pressure for the Brazilian real to appreciate against the U.S. dollar will grow.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One reason is an expected global weakening of the U.S. dollar because of continued loose monetary policy by the U.S. Federal Reserve Board, according to a study by economists at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to stem BRL appreciation this August and September has been as strong as in August and September 2010," the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  economists noted. "We see the scale of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  recently as supporting our case for BRL appreciation in the medium term."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Another reason to expect pressure for an appreciation of the Brazilian real is inflows from corporate bond issues. A number of companies, including banking giants Itau (ITUB, ITUB4.BR) and government-run mortgage bank Caixa Economica Federal, are planning bond issues. Those dollars will pour into the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market in the coming weeks, forcing either an appreciation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or additional heavy government \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , according to traders.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's government has signaled its strong intention to fight back against any significant appreciation, however. In a recent interview, Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guido Mantega\f28 \uc2 \f2  said a strong real would hurt exporters and manufacturers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tom Murphy\f28 \uc2 \f2  at tom.murphy@dowjones.com [ 06-11-12 1829GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Doku