\par\par \b \uc2 Latest Wave of Overseas Issues Could Pressure Brazil Real\b0\par\par\uc2 623 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 November 2012\par 19:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil companies tapping debt market because of low interest rates\par \par \uc2 --But inflows could lead to unwanted appreciation of Brazilian real\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may act to contain appreciation pressure on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Rogerio Jelmayer \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SAO PAULO--A heavy inflow of U.S. dollars from overseas bond issues by Brazilian companies could bring an unwanted appreciation of the Brazilian real against the greenback, triggering a new round of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 On Monday, a number of Brazilian companies set the tone, with nearly simultaneous news of overseas debt \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Banking giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Itau Unibanco Holding SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  (ITUB) is planning to issue overseas bonds due in 2023. Others include oil and gas company \f28 \uc2 \f2 Queiroz Galvao\f28 \uc2 \f2  and Cielo SA (CIOXY, CIEL3.BR), Brazil's largest credit-card company. Meatpacker \f28 \uc2 \f2 Marfrig\f28 \uc2 \f2  (MRRTY, MRFG3.BR) is expected to announce a bond issue, and accompanying international road show, in the next few days.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian companies are taking advantage of rock bottom international interest rates and low risk premiums for Brazil. The combination has brought record low yields on recent Brazilian debt issues.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "In the next few days, we could see a huge inflow of cash from these overseas bond issues," said Miriam Tavares, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  director at Sao Paulo's AGK brokerage. "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be very alert to this. I believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will use all of its instruments to defend the current trading range of BRL2.00 to BRL2.05 to-the-dollar."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian real has been trading in that narrow range since July. Much of the reason is because that is how Brazil's government wants it.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Officials, including Finance Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guido Mantega\f28 \uc2 \f2 , have argued that any abrupt appreciation of the Brazilian real against the U.S. dollar hurts exporters and manufacturers. In a recent interview, Mr. Mantega even admitted that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's policy of frequent market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  constitutes "a dirty float" of the nation's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the American dollar.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  often come at the rate of one or more per week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is likely to absorb these new inflows via reverse swap auctions, similar to those used in recent sessions," said Ms. Tavares.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Reverse swap auctions offer investors the opportunity to exchange dollar-linked contracts due at future dates for paper indexed to domestic interest rates. The auctions typically serve to strengthen the U.S. dollar against the Brazilian real by reducing the availability of dollar-hedging contracts in the market. By using them, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  avoids direct buying and selling of dollars.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At the end of October, when state-run bank Caixa Economica Federal raised $1.5 billion via a bond issue, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sold a total of around $3 billion in reverse swap contracts at two auctions, actions that helped keep the real within the tight trading band despite the heavy inflows.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 More Brazilian debt issues are likely, according to analysts.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With interest rates across the globe at historically low levels and Europe in crisis, global investors are showing an increased appetite for assets previously considered high in risk.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Currently, there is investor appetite even for small players, including Brazilian companies that are not rated investment grade but that can provide high yields for investors," said Rodrigo Fittipaldi, debt market director at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  bank in Sao Paulo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 From January through September, the most recent figures available, overseas bonds issues totaled $37.5 billion, almost the same value as for the entire year of 2011, some $38.5 billion, according to the Brazilian Financial and Capital Markets Association, or Anbima.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Rogerio Jelmayer at rogerio.jelmayer@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribe to WSJ: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2 \f2  [ 05-11-12 1810GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1833   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121105e8b50015x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
