\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  dips, Mexico peso hits 7-week low\b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Oktober 2012\par 16:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Hurricane Sandy shuts Wall St, cuts volumes in Latam\par \par \uc2 * Mexico peso weakens 0.67 pct, Brazil real off 0.31 pct\par \par \uc2 (Adds comments, changes dateline)\par \par \uc2 By Michael O'Boyle\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Oct 29 (Reuters) - Mexico's peso slumped to a seven-week low on Monday as uncertainty over a much-awaited bailout request by Spain weighed on demand for riskier assets such as Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Trading volumes were low as U.S. markets were closed due to the approach of Hurricane Sandy, which was expected to hit the U.S. East Coast later in the day.\par \par \uc2 Fears that Madrid would take too long to request a sovereign bailout increased after a \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymaker, \uc2 Ewald Nowotny\uc2 , said over the weekend that Spain should try to refinance itself before requesting aid.\par \par \uc2 Investors consider a Spanish bailout crucial to stopping the spreading of the euro zone debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 "The effect of the hurricane and considerations that the situation remains delicate in Europe, particularly Spain, all added up to feed more demand for safe-haven assets," said Eduardo Avila, an analyst at brokerage Monex in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso led losses in Latin America's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, dropping 0.67 percent to 13.0820 per dollar. The peso pared losses slightly after it hit its weakest intraday level since early September at 13.1095.\par \par \uc2 The peso posted slight gains on Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  warned it could raise interest rates if inflation pressures persist. Higher interest rates in Mexico would boost the attraction of its debt to yield-hungry investors.\par \par \uc2 But analysts on Monday said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to raise borrowing costs with looming risks of slowing growth and some analysts recommended taking advantage of a recent rise in Mexican yields to snap up cheaper bonds.\par \par \uc2 When a bond's yield rises, its price falls.\par \par \uc2 The annual inflation rate in Latin America's second-largest economy eased from a 2-1/2 year high of 4.77 percent in September to 4.64 percent in the first half of October and many economist think inflation could fall further in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 "These inflation pressures will pass, but it will take time," Avila said.\par \par \uc2 The yield on Mexico's benchmark 10-year peso bond\par \par \uc2 bid up 5 basis points to 5.55 percent.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the real weakened 0.31 percent to 2.0320 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Expectations of continued government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  have drastically reduced volumes and volatility in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, leaving the real in a narrow trading range of 2.02-2.05 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Investors expect the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may sell reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps at any moment to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at current levels, which government officials consider beneficial to exporters.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice last week with the sale of those swaps, or derivatives contracts that emulate the purchase of dollars in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2130 GMT\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %  year-to\par                                   change   date %\par                          Latest            change\par Brazil real                2.0320    -0.31    -8.11\par                                           \par Mexico peso               13.0820    -0.67     6.78\par                                           \par Argentina peso*            6.3300     0.79   -25.28\par                                           \par Chile peso               481.8000    -0.31     7.78\par                                           \par Colombia peso          1,830.5000    -0.14     5.89\par                                           \par Peru sol                   2.6020    -0.15     3.65\par                                           \par * Argentine peso's rate between                    \par brokerages                                  \par                                                  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Walter Brandimarte; Editing by Phil Berlowitz)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | U | C | O | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121101e8at0013k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
