\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Closes Little Changed Against Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 432 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Oktober 2012\par 21:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's real chalked up a very slight gain against the dollar in steady trading Wednesday, as major stock indexes stopped bleeding after the steep declines of previous sessions.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading in Sao Paulo at BRL2.0250 to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, barely stronger than Tuesday's close of BRL2.0255.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's steadiness reflected a relative calm day in world financial markets. The Dow Jones Industrial Average, after sinking more than 1.8% on Tuesday, was slightly lower in afternoon trading.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's real historically tracks other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and key stock indexes but has hardly moved in recent months. Local authorities, seeking to prop up a flagging industrial sector, have used taxes, rhetoric and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market this year to wrestle \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's once-volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a range of about BRL2.0 to BRL2.05 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "The exchange rate as I see it is frozen," said Joao Medeiros, a partner at Sao Paulo's Pioneer Corretora. "We haven't ever had such a rigid freeze, as the one we have today in Brazil."\par \par \uc2 Brazil adopted a floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime in 1999, after maintaining an official peg to the dollar when it launched the real in 1994. Local authorities, for their part, haven't disclosed any official change in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2 , in an interview published Wednesday by financial daily Valor Economico, highlighted that the exchange rate "is not fixed."\par \par \uc2 "Our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system is a dirty float, same as everybody," Mr. Mantega said. Brazilian officials consider the loose monetary policies that have lingered for years in the U.S. and other developed countries to be a form of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation.\par \par \uc2 But with annual inflation running more than a full percentage point above the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 4.5% target, some economists say authorities may have to loosen the reins on the real, assuming they want to keep interest rates at record low levels.\par \par \uc2 "Were inflationary pressures to intensify and drive inflation above 5.50% at some point during 2013, then the authorities may choose to soften the current hard \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  stance," \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  economist Alberto Ramos said this week in a note. That would allow the real's range "to restrike at a moderately lower level in order to temporarily anchor the inflation dynamics and delay and/or moderate the use of rates to anchor inflation."\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 24-10-12 1939GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121024e8ao0011x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
