\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  falls on Spain,  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 660 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2012\par 17:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \uc2 Moody's\uc2  cuts 5 Spanish regions, sparking risk aversion\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso drops nearly 1 pct; Brazil real down 0.1 pct\par \par \uc2 * Chilean peso loses 1.18 pct\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  with sale of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps\par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, background, quotes)\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte and Alexandra Alper\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO/MEXICO CITY Oct 23 (Reuters) - The Mexican and Chilean \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped on Tuesday as a credit downgrade of five Spanish regions and weak earnings at U.S. companies reinforced fears of anemic global growth and a deepening euro-zone crisis.\par \par \uc2 Spain's borrowing costs spiked after the \uc2 Moody's\uc2  ratings downgrade, which included the economically important but deeply indebted Catalonia region.\par \par \uc2 "Markets are negative on the unsettling European news," said Rodrigo Sarria, a trader at Celfin Capital in Santiago.\par \par \uc2 Investors are waiting for signs that Spain will request a sovereign bailout, something seen as a crucial step to stop the spreading of the euro zone debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso dropped 0.92 percent to 12.97 per dollar. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  briefly broke past the psychological 13 per dollar level to a nearly six-week low.\par \par \uc2 The Chilean peso fell to a two-month low in its biggest one-day percentage loss in four months. The peso lost 1.18 percent to close at 482.70 per greenback.\par \par \uc2 A drop in the price of copper, Chile's main export product, further pressured the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market for the first time in more than two weeks to weaken the real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The real slipped 0.1 percent to 2.0265 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  came after a series of small gains led the real to close on Monday at 2.0244 per dollar, its strongest level since Oct. 4 and close to the 2 per dollar level that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been seen defending.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivative contracts that emulate the purchase of dollars in the futures market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the sale was merely intended to roll over similar contracts that expire on Nov. 1.\par \par \uc2 Traders speculated that the bank could act again because it sold only a little more than half of the 60,000 contracts it offered in an auction -- not enough to roll over all the 59,800 reverse swaps that expire next week.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 17,000 swaps maturing on Dec. 3, 2012, and 16,000 contracts maturing Jan. 2, 2013, it said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso weakened to 13.01 per dollar, its weakest since Sept. 13, but recovered to close out the session in stronger territory. Market watchers said they did not expect the weakening trend to continue.\par \par \uc2 "I think the market is expecting a better close to the year in the U.S. economy....That will have a positive impact on the exchange rate," said Jorge Gordillo, an analyst at CI Banco in Mexico City.\par \par \uc2 Gordillo said he expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to strengthen on Thursday or Friday back past the 12.90 level on the release of key U.S. data, which has been stronger in September and October.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. government will release data on durable good orders for September on Thursday and third-quarter gross domestic product numbers on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 21:00 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                           daily %  year-t\par                                    change   -date\par                     Latest                      %\par                                            change\par Brazil real           2.0265          -0.10   -7.80\par                                            \par Mexico peso          12.9700          -0.92    7.71\par                                            \par Argentina peso*       6.3000          -0.32  -24.92\par                                            \par Chile peso          482.7000          -1.18    7.58\par                                            \par Colombia peso      1,816.150          -0.44    6.73\par                                            \par Peru sol              2.5820          -0.15    4.45\par                                            \par * Argentine peso's rate                            \par between brokerages                           \par                                                  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Moises Avila in Santiago; Editing by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Leslie Adler\f28 \uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | C | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121026e8an0014m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
