\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Weakens Slightly on  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Europe Worries\b0\par\par\uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2012\par 20:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real exits active trading at BRL2.0255/dollar versus BRL2.0235 Monday\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  early in trading, selling \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sells enough swap contracts to cover Nov. 1 expiry\par \par \uc2 --European worries, weak euro and lower commodities prices also weigh\par \par \uc2 By \uc2 Tom Murphy\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--The Brazilian real weakened slightly against the U.S. dollar Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market through a \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auction.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0255 to the dollar, weaker against the Monday close of BRL2.0235, according to Tullet Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in the first minutes of trading with a so-called reverse swap auction.\par \par \uc2 The reverse swap auction allows investors to exchange dollar-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  contracts for paper indexed to domestic interest rates. Typically, the reverse swap auction supports the dollar against the real by removing dollar-hedged contracts from the market.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has used reverse swap auctions frequently in recent months to help avoid any significant appreciation of the real against the dollar. Brazilian officials have said a strong real hurts exporters and manufacturers.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  held a reverse swap auction Tuesday for two reasons.\par \par \uc2 The first reason was to cover an upcoming Nov. 1 expiry of dollar-linked contracts. The expiry involves some $3 billion equivalent in contracts. At Tuesday's reverse swap auction, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the equivalent of $1.648 billion in contracts. That, plus an early October reverse swap auction worth nearly $1.3 billion, will be enough to negate effects of the Nov. 1 expiry, traders said.\par \par \uc2 The second reason was to help counter effects of recent U.S. dollar inflows, including overseas corporate bond issues.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is mopping up U.S. dollar liquidity and maintaining equilibrium in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate," said Sidnei Nehme, director of Sao Paulo's NGO brokerage.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Nehme noted that government figures released Tuesday showed steady net inflows of dollars during the first three weeks of October. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  figures showed net inflows of $1.59 billion, up sharply from $647 million in the first three weeks of September.\par \par \uc2 Traders added, however, that the Brazilian government will have little difficulty avoiding any significant appreciation of the real.\par \par \uc2 "There is virtually no chance the Brazilian real will be able to free itself from the current narrow trading range," said Mario Battistel, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sao Paulo's Fair brokerage.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's fire power includes both swap auctions and snap auctions at which it buys and sells large volumes of dollars on the spot market. The finance ministry, meanwhile, has used other tools in recent years to combat the unwanted appreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These have included high taxes on short-term investment positions.\par \par \uc2 In any case, according to Mr. Nehme, heavy new inflows of dollars aren't likely in the coming months. He noted that Tuesday's government data also showed a persistent current account deficit, during September some $2.6 billion.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real was also pressured Tuesday by a gloomy international outlook. Continued worries about the European debt crisis led to a weakening of the euro against the dollar and a decline in commodities prices. Stocks also lost ground, including in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 Lower commodities prices hit the Brazilian real directly because they translate into declining export revenue.\par \par \uc2 Write to \uc2 Tom Murphy\uc2  at tom.murphy@dowjones.com [ 23-10-12 1855GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121023e8an000y7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
