\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weaker Early As Market Mulls Inflation, Mood Abroad\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 379 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2012\par 13:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA -- Brazil's real weakened slightly in early trading Monday as investors weighed prospects for dollar inflows amid signs of continued strong inflation locally and renewed risk aversion in markets abroad.\par \par \uc2 As of 7:40 EDT, the real traded at BRL2.0270 to the dollar after ending at BRL2.0262 to the dollar Friday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 In a \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  weekly market survey released early Monday, expectations for IPCA consumer price inflation inched up slightly after 12-month inflation posted late last week for mid-October rose to 5.56% from 5.31% the previous month under the influence of high food prices. Brazil has set a year-end inflation target of 4.5%.\par \par \uc2 The still-strong inflation has served as a factor to limit forecasts of possible continued interest rate cuts locally following 5.25 percentage points of rate reductions made over the past 12 months.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, factors abroad continued to offset expectations of growing inflows as markets showed heightened investor uncertainties late last week over prospects for a recovery of the global economy.\par \par \uc2 With strong selloffs overseas Friday, prices of key commodities sold by Brazil and other emerging markets fell early Monday, weighing against the likelihood of strong trade inflows in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Further, investors have continued to look toward the resolution of a nagging debt crisis in Europe and signals the U.S. can overcome sluggish growth, before resuming heavier investments in Brazil.\par \par \uc2 And with current moderate local demand, analysts expect Brazil's government may continue to carry out efforts to support local industry through stimulus measures and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in recent weeks, through reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, though some market players feel the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  could try to encourage further weakening of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a current "band" seen between BRL2.00 and BRL2.05 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  market survey released Monday shows the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ending 2012 at around BRL2.01 to the dollar and remaining around that level through the end of 2013.\par \par \uc2 -Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 22-10-12 1149GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121022e8am000pc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
