\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Mexican peso up on Spain hope, Brazil real flat\b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Oktober 2012\par 14:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Spain elections seen as a boost to PM austerity drive\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real flat with traders on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  watch\par \par \uc2 * Mexican peso gains 0.25 pct, Chilean peso little changed\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Oct 22 (Reuters) - The Mexican peso gained early on Monday on renewed hopes that Spain would request financial aid, while the Brazilian real was flat as investors awaited a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Mexican \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained 0.25 percent after the outcome of Spain's regional elections was seen as a boost to Prime Minister Mariano Rajoy's austerity drive.\par \par \uc2 The results rekindled hopes Madrid would soon request a sovereign bailout, seen by investors as crucial to mitigate the region's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, however, the real was unchanged at 2.0273 per dollar as investors expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to soon roll over some $3 billion in reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps that expire on Nov. 1.\par \par \uc2 The contracts, which mimic the purchase of dollars in the futures market, were sold by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early September to stop the real from strengthening past 2 per dollar - a level the bank has been defending since early July to support Brazilian exporters.\par \par \uc2 "With the real still at the lower end of the broad 2.0-2.1 reais per dollar range, we assign a high probability that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will choose to roll over these maturities," Flavia Cattan-Naslausky, a strategist with RBS, said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 1230 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                          daily %    YTD %\par                                   change   change\par                          Latest           \par Brazil real                2.0273     0.00    -7.83\par                                           \par Mexico peso               12.8681     0.25     8.56\par                                           \par Argentina peso*            6.2900     0.48   -24.80\par                                           \par Chile peso               474.8000    -0.04     9.37\par                                           \par Peru sol                   2.5780    -0.04     4.62\par                                           \par * Argentine peso's rate between                    \par brokerages                                  \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Reporting by Walter Brandimarte; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  | ABN | D | E | RBN | M | NAT | C | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121025e8am0014z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
