\par\par \b \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgrades Banco BVA's deposits and debt to Ca; continues review for downgrade\b0\par\par\uc2 2,541 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Oktober 2012\par \uc2 Moody's Investors Service Press Release\par \uc2 MOODPR\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012   \par \par \uc2 Moody's Investors Service\uc2  has today lowered the baseline credit assessment of Banco BVA S.A. (BVA) to ca from caa1, that maps from an E bank financial strength rating (BFSR) assigned to the bank. Concurrently, \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgraded the bank's long-term global local and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit ratings to Ca from Caa1 as well as its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt rating to Ca from Caa1. The long-term Brazilian national scale deposit rating was also downgraded to Ca.br from Caa1.br.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  also maintained the review for possible downgrade on all deposits and debt ratings. Today's action follows the announcement that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  has declared \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on BVA.\par \par \uc2 RATING RATIONALE\par \par \uc2 The rating downgrades followed the announcement by Brazil's regulatory authorities on October 19, 2012 that a direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was declared on BVA because of its weak financial position and inability to comply with \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  regulations. The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  process entails the interruption of all of BVA's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  while the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  conducts a thorough examination of the bank's financial condition and capacity to repay all of its obligations.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  assigned one of its executives to oversee the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  process. BVA's former executives are no longer allowed to manage the bank. The properties, possessions and financial resources of both former executives and BVA's controllers were blocked by force of law.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  notes that the downgrade and continuing review for further downgrade of BVA's global local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit rating reflects the bank's highly speculative standalone financial strength and the uncertainties regarding the resolution of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  process, with a high likelihood of liquidation and default on uninsured obligations. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Ca global scale rating implies a 55% loss.\par \par \uc2 The last rating action on BVA occurred on September 26, 2012, when \uc2 Moody's\uc2  downgraded BVA's standalone BFSR to E from E+, and lowered its baseline credit assessment to caa1. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  also downgraded the long-term global local and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit ratings and the long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  senior debt rating to Caa1 from B2. The Brazilian national scale deposit ratings were lowered to Caa1.br and BR-4 from Ba1.br and BR-3, long- and short-term, respectively. The short-term global local and foreign deposit ratings were not affected. All deposit and debt ratings were placed on review for downgrade; the outlook on the standalone BFSR was stable.\par \par \uc2 The principal methodology used in rating this bank was "\uc2 Moody's\uc2  Consolidated Global Bank Rating Methodology" published on 29 June 2012. Please see the Credit Policy page on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.moodys.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.moodys.com}}}\uc2  for a copy of this methodology.\par \par \uc2 Moody's\uc2  National Scale Ratings (NSRs) are intended as relative measures of creditworthiness among debt issues and issuers within a country, enabling market participants to better differentiate relative risks. NSRs differ from \uc2 Moody's\uc2  global scale ratings in that they are not globally comparable with the full universe of \uc2 Moody's\uc2  rated entities, but only with NSRs for other rated debt issues and issuers within the same country. NSRs are designated by a ".nn" country modifier signifying the relevant country, as in ".mx" for Mexico. For further information on \uc2 Moody's\uc2  approach to national scale ratings, please refer to \uc2 Moody's\uc2  Rating Methodology published in October 2012 entitled "Mapping \uc2 Moody's\uc2  National Scale Ratings to Global Scale Ratings".\par \par \uc2 Banco BVA S.A. is headquartered in S\u227\'00\'E3o Paulo, Brazil. As of December 2011, the bank had total assets of approximately R$6.74 billion (US$3.61 billion) and equity of R$747 million (US$401 million).\par \par \uc2 The following ratings were downgraded and continue on review for downgrade:\par \par \uc2 Long-term global local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit rating: to Ca from Caa1\par \par \uc2 Long-term Foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit rating: to Ca from Caa1\par \par \uc2 Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  senior unsecured debt program rating: to (P)Ca from (P)Caa1\par \par \uc2 Long-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  senior unsecured debt rating: to Ca from Caa1\par \par \uc2 Long-term Brazilian national scale deposit rating: to Ca.br from Caa1.br\par \par \uc2 The following ratings remained unchanged:\par \par \uc2 Bank Financial Strength Rating: E, stable outlook\par \par \uc2 Short-term global local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit rating: Not Prime\par \par \uc2 Short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  deposit rating: Not Prime\par \par \uc2 Short-term foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt program rating: (P)Not Prime\par \par \uc2 Short-term Brazilian national scale deposit rating: BR-4\par \par \uc2 REGULATORY DISCLOSURES\par \par \uc2 The Global Scale Credit Ratings on this press release that are issued by one of \uc2 Moody's\uc2  affiliates outside the EU are endorsed by \uc2 Moody's Investors Service Ltd\uc2 ., One Canada Square, \uc2 Canary Wharf\uc2 , London E 14 5FA, UK, in accordance with Art.4 paragraph 3 of the Regulation (EC) No 1060/2009 on Credit Rating Agencies. Further information on the EU endorsement status and on the \uc2 Moody's\uc2  office that has issued a particular Credit Rating is available on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.moodys.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.moodys.com}}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For ratings issued on a program, series or category/class of debt, this announcement provides relevant regulatory disclosures in relation to each rating of a subsequently issued bond or note of the same series or category/class of debt or pursuant to a program for which the ratings are derived exclusively from existing ratings in accordance with \uc2 Moody's\uc2  rating practices. For ratings issued on a support provider, this announcement provides relevant regulatory disclosures in relation to the rating action on the support provider and in relation to each particular rating action for securities that derive their credit ratings from the support provider's credit rating. For provisional ratings, this announcement provides relevant regulatory disclosures in relation to the provisional rating assigned, and in relation to a definitive rating that may be assigned subsequent to the final issuance of the debt, in each case where the transaction structure and terms have not changed prior to the assignment of the definitive rating in a manner that would have affected the rating. For further information please see the ratings tab on the issuer/entity page for the respective issuer on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.moodys.