\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Weakens Slightly in Early Trading Following Report\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 309 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2012\par 14:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real weakened slightly in early trading Thursday after the minutes of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest interest-rate meeting signaled a slow process of recovery ahead.\par \par \uc2 As of 0840 ET, the real traded at BRL2.0291 to the dollar after ending at BRL2.0288 to the dollar Wednesday, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the market was closely following signs from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on whether the institution could alter the path of interest rates as part of its efforts to stimulate growth and control inflation.\par \par \uc2 In the minutes of its latest meeting, the bank said it expected to leave the country's benchmark Selic interest rate at a historic low of 7.25% for a "sufficiently prolonged" period of time to allow for a recovery of the local economy.\par \par \uc2 At the rate meeting last week, the bank's rate committee voted by a margin of 5-to-3 to cut the rate by a quarter percentage point, noting local inflation would continue to converge toward its 4.5% annual target in a "non-linear" manner.\par \par \uc2 Investors were also closely monitoring factors abroad, including a meeting of European authorities to discuss bailout mechanisms for regional governments seeking recovery from an ongoing fiscal crisis.\par \par \uc2 Also affecting the real Thursday were trends in China, where recent stable growth figures signaled good prospects for continued firm sales of Brazilian commodities in that region.\par \par \uc2 Investors, meanwhile, remained on the lookout for signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local markets by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government, as local authorities in recent sessions continued to pledge an active stance to prevent the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening beyond a level of BRL2.00 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com. [ 18-10-12 1252GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121018e8ai000sp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
