\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Ends Stronger as Market Sees More Dollar Inflows\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gerald Jeffris   \par \uc2 357 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 2012\par 22:07\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--Brazil's real climbed slightly to end stronger Thursday as investors continued to bet on incoming investment dollars ahead following the release of details from the country's latest interest rate meeting.\par \par \uc2 The real exited regular trading at BRL2.0270 to the dollar after ending at BRL2.0288 to the dollar Wednesday, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset.\par \par \uc2 Traders noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  began the session on a weakening trend amid concerns the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate decision was the harbinger of a continued slow local recovery.\par \par \uc2 In the minutes of its latest rate meeting, the bank said it expected to leave the country's benchmark Selic interest rate at a historic low of 7.25% for a "sufficiently prolonged" period to allow for a recovery in activity.\par \par \uc2 At the meeting last week, the bank's rate committee voted 5 to 3 to cut the rate by a quarter percentage point.\par \par \uc2 Overseas factors, however, were also influencing the market. Among those were U.S. jobless claims, which surpassed expectations by rising 46,000 in the second week of October. The latest weak data in the U.S., helped convince investors that loose monetary conditions abroad should continue to favor returns and incoming foreign investment in Brazil, where rates still remain well above those elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 With Brazil's latest rate meeting minutes, analysts said the bank signaled it could eventually return to a tightening cycle by the end of next year.\par \par \uc2 "The balance of risks for growth and inflation would likely justify a moderate normalization of monetary conditions by at least 100bp-150bp sometime in 2H2013," said \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2  economist Alberto Ramos in a note.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , meanwhile, refrained from \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market Thursday, despite some strengthening of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Analysts, however, said they believe the bank may still jump back into the market with an auction of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps if the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  threatens to strengthen beyond BRL2.00 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 18-10-12 2007GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121018e8ai0010l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
