\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Closes Weaker Following Reverse-Swap Auction\b0\par\par\uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Oktober 2012\par 23:16\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil's real ends weaker after sale of reverse-swap contracts\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was not a surprise, says trader\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real exits active trading at BRL2.0293 to the U.S. dollar\par \par \uc2 By Luciana Magalhaes\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO-- The Brazilian real closed weaker to the dollar Friday after the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold reverse-swap contracts to deter the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation.\par \par \uc2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0293 to the U.S. dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, after Thursday closing price at BRL2.0167.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold the equivalent to $1.29 billion in reverse swap contracts Friday. Such auctions give the investors a chance to exchange dollar-linked bonds for paper indexed to domestic interest rates. They tend to support the dollar against the real by removing dollar-hedged contracts from the market.\par \par \uc2 The real lost strength immediately following the auction. Before the announcement of the auction, the real was trading at BRL2.0199 to the dollar. After the auction, the real was trading at BRL2.0229 to the dollar. In the morning, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded as strong as BRL2.0154 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "When I saw the real trading at around BRL2.016, I expected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Mauro Araujo, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  director at Brazilian brokerage Vision Corretora. "The Brazilian authorities clearly don't want to see the real stronger than something around BRL2.020 to the dollar."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and declarations from government officials aiming to protect local exporters have kept the real in a tight trading range between BRL2.00 and BRL2.05 in recent months.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had weakened to around BRL2.0190 but recovered the loss after the U.S. Labor Department reported the unemployment rate fell to 7.8% in September from 8.1% in the previous month, the lowest level since January 2009. The U.S. economy added 114,000 jobs last month, according to the government's monthly survey of employers.\par \par \uc2 "Next week, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will be paying attention to the monetary-policy meeting," said Mr. Araujo. "We believe, given the inflation concerns, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be conservative."\par \par \uc2 As Mr. Araujo does, many economists expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep its baseline Selic rate at the current 7.5%, a record low that followed a yearlong easing cycle that brought rates down from 12.5% in August 2011.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's consumer price index rose at a quicker pace in September as drought in Brazil and the U.S. caused food prices to jump, the Brazilian Institute of Geography and Statistics, or IBGE, said Friday.\par \par \uc2 Write to Luciana Magalhaes at luciana.magalhaes@dowjones.com [ 05-10-12 2116GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020121005e8a5000yf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
