\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  firms on US data, upside seen limited\b0\par\par\uc2 631 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2012\par 23:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Positive U.S. data raises hopes ahead of payrolls report\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , global growth worries to limit gains -poll\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real firms 0.24 pct; Mexico peso up 0.57 pct\par \par \uc2 (Add comments, poll results)\par \par \uc2 By Jean Arce and Patricia Duarte\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, Oct 4 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed on Thursday after U.S. labor market data helped ease concerns about slowing growth in one of the region's top trading partners, but a Reuters poll showed further gains are likely to be limited.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso jumped to a two-week high after data showed fewer Americans than expected filed for new unemployment benefits last week, leading to hopes that Friday's closely watched non-farm payrolls report would show improvement.\par \par \uc2 Mexico sends nearly 80 percent of its exports to the United States, which is a major trading partner across Latin America.\par \par \uc2 "People seem to be anticipating a good jobs report tomorrow," said Rafael Camarena, an economist at Santander in Mexico City. "A good employment number would push off the fears of a deeper slowdown."\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso strengthened 0.57 percent to trade at 12.7525 per U.S. dollar.\par \par \uc2 Also supporting Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were renewed hopes for a much-awaited Spanish bailout. Expectations grew after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  confirmed the bank is ready to buy bonds of debt-ridden euro zone countries.\par \par \uc2 Concerns about Europe's debt troubles have repeatedly hammered riskier assets around the world this year, but concerns that Europe could trigger a global financial crisis have faded since Draghi promised to support euro zone bond markets in late July.\par \par \uc2 But Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have limited room for gains in the year ahead as governments fight the massive dollar inflows expected after the latest round of stimulus from the U.S. Federal Reserve, a Reuters poll found on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso's gains are expected to be limited in the coming year, the poll showed, on concerns about high local asset prices and a weak global economy. Mexican peso-denominated bonds and stocks are trading near record high prices.\par \par \uc2 REAL GAINS\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real firmed 0.24 percent to 2.0175 per dollar at the local close, edging closer to the 2 per dollar level that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is seen defending.\par \par \uc2 Since early July, the real's volatility has been constrained by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Brazilian government has battled against the real's strength in recent years in an attempt to protect the competitiveness of exports.\par \par \uc2 Economists now expect the real to remain stable around the 2 per dollar level for at the least six months, the Reuters survey found.\par \par \uc2 "If the dollar falls, we know the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will act," said Mario Battistel, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at brokerage Fair.\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso gained about 0.19 percent to trade at 472.50 per dollar as prices of copper, the country's main export, rose.\par \par \uc2 Analysts are speculating that Chile could soon join Brazil, Colombia and Peru in fighting \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains if the peso firms much past 470 per dollar. Mexico is not expected to step up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2045 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             daily %  year-to-\par                                      change     ate %\par                            Latest              change\par Brazil real                  2.0175      0.24     -7.39\par                                              \par Mexico peso                 12.7525      0.57      9.54\par                                              \par Argentina peso*              6.1700      1.30    -23.34\par                                              \par Chile peso                 472.5000      0.19      9.90\par                                              \par Colombia peso            1,795.2500      0.40      7.97\par                                              \par Peru sol                     2.5930      0.19      4.01\par                                              \par * Argentine peso's rate between                        \par brokerages                                     \par                                                      \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Writing by Michael O'Boyle; Editing by Leslie Adler)\f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-LATAM/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (REPEATS) (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | M | RBN | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121007e8a4000cw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
