\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-POLL-Brazil real seen stable at 2/dollar for months\b0\par\par\uc2 780 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Oktober 2012\par 18:02\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers with no change to text)\par \par \uc2 * For poll data see\par \par \uc2 * Real seen gaining a mere 2.5 percent in a year\par \par \uc2 * Gov't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , China, euro zone seen weighing on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 By Walter Brandimarte\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO, Oct 4 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market have helped convince economists that the real will remain stable around 2 per dollar for at least the next six months, a Reuters survey found on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Expectations that U.S. monetary stimulus would drive strong dollar inflows to Brazil have also given way to growing concerns about China and the euro zone, adding to bets on a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Economists now expect the real to trade at 1.97 per dollar in one year, only 2.5 percent stronger than its current level, according to the median forecast of 32 financial institutions in Brazil and abroad.\par \par \uc2 The real currently hovers around 2.02 per greenback, more than 16 percent weaker from late February. Only a couple of months ago, economists had forecast it would recover to 1.96 by February of 2013 and to 1.92 by August.\par \par \uc2 "The world has changed, commodity prices have changed, China has changed, and we also see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  more actively," said Dalton Gardiman, chief economist with \uc2 Bradesco\uc2  BBI, the investment banking arm of \uc2 Banco Bradesco\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Altogether, those factors totally justify a weaker real in the next few months," he added.\par \par \uc2 Worries about the magnitude of China's economic slowdown, which is likely to extend to a seventh consecutive quarter, have been tempering investors' bets on higher commodities prices, and on Brazil's trade performance as a result.\par \par \uc2 Adding to the cloudy global scenario is a persistent euro-zone debt crisis that is likely to trigger regular bouts of capital flight to dollar-denominated assets.\par \par \uc2 Dollar outflows from Brazil could also grow as local companies honor debt payments on a large number of bonds they issued in international capital markets, noted Marjorie Hernandez, Latin American strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 "All of a sudden the picture is a lot more neutral (for the real). We see slight dollar outflows," she said.\par \par \uc2 Even if all those factors turn out to be not as bad as feared, investors would still need to surmount a "wall" of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  measures that the Brazilian government has pledged to put in place if needed.\par \par \uc2 "Even if the international scenario improves next year, which I don't think is likely, it's still difficult to see the real strengthening too much because the government has been using administrative measures to curb \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains," said Darwin Dib, chief economist at CM Capital Markets, a brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Government sources have recently told Reuters that the first line of defense against undesirable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains would be \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions and dollar purchases by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . If that is not enough, the Finance Ministry would join the fight with targeted tax hikes on capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 The measures should ensure the real remains weaker than 2 per dollar, a level considered beneficial to exporters.\par \par \uc2 The plan is part of President Dilma Rousseff's campaign against what she has called a "monetary tsunami" caused by the expansionary monetary policies in the United States and Europe, which can potentially hurt Brazilian exporters by driving up the value of the real.\par \par \uc2 But many economists now believe markets have already priced in the impact of the latest rounds of monetary stimulus in the developed world, removing a key driver for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains in Latin America.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, that leaves inflation as one of the main arguments for a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Brazil's 12-month inflation currently runs nearly 1 percentage point higher than the center of the government's 4.5 percent target. If price indexes continue to go up in the next few months, policymakers could choose to let the real strengthen in order to make imports cheaper.\par \par \uc2 That might be a more palatable alternative than raising interest rates, which Rousseff's government has lowered to an all-time low of 7.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Still, many economists say there are other options to put a lid on inflation.\par \par \uc2 "That is going to be their last option before raising interest rates. Their priority will be (sales) tax cuts," said Dib from CM Capital Markets.\par \par \uc2 (For other stories from the poll see )\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Silvio Cascione in Sao Paulo and Michael O'Boyle in Mexico City; Editing by Chizu Nomiyama)\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -BRAZIL/POLL  (REPEAT) | ABN | D | NAT | E | U | RBN | M | O | OIL | C | GRO | MTL | SOF   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020121004e8a40011c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
