\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Hamilton:  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  to Continue  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  as Needed\b0\par\par\uc2 154 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2012\par 18:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 BRASILIA--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to continue \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as part of its efforts to limit \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility, bank economic policy director Carlos Hamilton Araujo said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 "We've \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market recently and certainly we'll continue to do so," he said.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has entered the market recently with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions as part of the country's efforts to hold it at levels that will aid local industries and contain inflation pressure.\par \par \uc2 Despite the bank's recent use of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap auctions, the director declined to rule out spot market auctions if conditions permit. "As market conditions allow us to continue reinforcing our reserves, we'll do so," he said.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's foreign reserves currently stand at $378.5 billion.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gerald Jeffris at gerald.jeffris@dowjones.com [ 09-27-12 1215ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020120927e89r00056\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
