\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil Real Closes Stronger, But Tough Talk Limits Gains\b0\par\par\uc2 745 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 September 2012\par 21:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains not tracking bigger movements overseas, traders say\par \par \uc2 --Real remains rangebound between BRL2.00 and BRL2.05 on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  concerns\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real exits active trading at BRL2.0297 to the greenback\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeff Fick \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RIO DE JANEIRO--The Brazilian real closed stronger against the U.S. dollar Thursday, but failed to track bigger overseas gains versus the greenback as \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  concerns kept the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  locked into its recent trading range.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0297 to the U.S. dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. That was stronger from Wednesday's closing price fix at BRL2.0320 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Nothing has changed, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Brazil is at a standstill," said Silvio Campos Neto, an economist at the Tendencias consultants group in Sao Paulo. "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate here has been very stable at current levels."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and recent government rhetoric have kept the real trading between BRL2.00 and BRL2.05 in recent months. While officials have continued to cite the need to ward off volatility for various \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and other measures, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has made it clear that the government is comfortable with the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at current levels because the real is weak enough to support local manufacturers and exporters without affecting inflation, traders said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's economic policy director, Carlos Hamilton Araujo, reaffirmed the government's intent Thursday. "We've \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the market recently and certainly we'll continue to do so," Mr. Araujo said. Recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  action has been focused on swap auctions, but Mr. Araujo didn't discount the use of spot-market auctions in the future.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "As market conditions allow us to continue reinforcing our reserves, we'll do so," Mr. Araujo said. Brazil's foreign reserves currently stand at $378.5 billion.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market shrugged off news from overseas that actually had other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  performing better against the buck, traders noted. China, Brazil's largest trading partner, injected a record amount of liquidity into its financial system this week, adding nearly $58 billion this week--including $8 billion overnight. While the move was directed at softening seasonal tightness in China's banking system, it could have a positive impact on Brazilian exports to the country.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Europe, meanwhile, moved closer to a firmer resolution of its ongoing debt troubles. Greece's three-party coalition agreed on most of the austerity measures required to receive the next tranche of bailout funds, while Spain unveiled a 2013 budget that included spending cuts and other tough measures aimed at reducing the country's deficit.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Around the world, the U.S. dollar depreciated because the moves alleviated risk concerns," Mr. Campos said. "But here, the movement [versus the dollar] was very small. [The real] is not tracking what the dollar is doing overseas."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Complicating Thursday's session was the month-end battle to set the average daily \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate used to settle futures contracts, known as the Ptax. Long- and short-position holders typically engage in a tug-of-war to influence the reference rate, adding a measure of volatility to trading at the end of each month.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could be tempted to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets should the real more closely approach the BRL2.02 mark, Durval Correa of Sao Paulo's Multi-Money brokerage said that he expected the bank to remain on the sidelines through the end of the week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real will likely continue trading in its recent range between BRL2.00 and BRL2.05 to the dollar, Mr. Correa said. "Apparently everyone is happy" with the real at current levels, Mr. Correa said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't feel like we're going to see any big changes in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate," Mr. Correa said. "The real is going to stay where it is and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is going to administer the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . If the real strengthens, it will sell dollars. If the real weakens, it will buy dollars."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The local market is currently in equilibrium, Mr. Correa said. Local banks are shorting the dollar, while funds are holding long positions, he added. That caused just a few sharp movements in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market that are largely related to light trading volume.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 --Gerald Jeffris in Brasilia contributed to this article.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Write to Jeff Fick at jeff.fick@dowjones.com [ 27-09-12 1926GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120927e89r00100\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
