\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Brazil may fire up tax artillery in ' \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  war'\b0\par\par\uc2 834 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2012\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Finance Minister says ready to act to keep lid on real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * Mantega says may ramp up short-term capital controls\par \par \uc2 * Tensions resurface over new U.S. monetary stimulus\par \par \uc2 * Brazil has taxed some foreign inflows since 2009\par \par \uc2 (Adds rising economic discord between U.S. and Brazil)\par \par \uc2 By Ana Nicolaci da Costa and Sujata Rao\par \par \uc2 LONDON, Sept 21 (Reuters) - Brazil threatened on Friday a further clampdown on speculative foreign capital, firing a warning shot in a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war" its finance minister blamed on money-printing by Western central banks.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Guido Mantega\uc2  said Brazil would not allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real, to strengthen as a result of aggressive monetary stimulus by the United States and other developed nations.\par \par \uc2 "If necessary ... we have (the option) of short-term capital taxes," he told reporters on the sidelines of an Economist conference in London.\par \par \uc2 Mantega's comments reflect growing tension between the South American nation and the United States over its lax monetary policy, which Brazilian officials blame for an avalanche of cheap imports crippling local producers.\par \par \uc2 Since 2009, the Brazilian government has introduced a number of measures intended to curb excess inflows of foreign investors' dollars but recently reduced their scope after the real weakened.\par \par \uc2 Brazil shocked investors in October of that year by taxing some categories of foreign capital flowing into stocks and bonds. It said at the time that some of the flows constituted hot money and were harming the economy.\par \par \uc2 Brazil has also raised duties on dozens of foreign-made goods to help a local industry struggling with a stronger real as well as some of the world's highest input costs.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Trade Representative Ron Kirk's calls for Brazil to reconsider plans for more tariff increases prompted a stinging response from Brasilia on Thursday. In a letter, the Brazilian government said the hike was a legitimate tool unlike the "illegal subsidization of farm products by the United States, which impact Brazil and other developing countries." ID:nL1E8KK9QE]\par \par \uc2 Mantega has become one of the fiercest critics of the asset buying programmes that Western central banks have been using to shore up their economies, accusing them of in effect devaluing their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost competitiveness.\par \par \uc2 The real held steady around 2.0245 per dollar for the fourth consecutive session on Friday following Mantega's threats to ramp up capital controls. His remarks added to the perception that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will keep \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the real nears the level of 2 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Some of the extra funds generated by quantitative easing (QE) have in the past found their way into emerging markets, lured by higher interest rates and yields, driving gains in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  including the real and Indonesia's rupiah.\par \par \uc2 Mantega said the U.S. Federal Reserve's decision this month to embark on a third round of bond-buying, followed by a similar move by Japan, would revive global "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars" by forcing other countries to act to protect their own economies.\par \par \uc2 "(The United States and Japan) will be stimulating the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  wars as (they) will lead all countries also to pursue these wars," Mantega said. "It's natural other countries will defend themselves."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 BRAZIL CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTIONS\b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has also \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to hold the real near the 2-per-dollar level via billions of dollars in reverse swaps. It has also cut interest rates to a record low of 7.5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Mantega told the conference there would be no let up in this process.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will buy more reserves, we already have a very high level of reserves and we will purchase more if there is a strong offer of dollars in the Brazilian economy," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We will do more reverse-swapping ... we won't allow our economy to become uncompetitive."\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian economy - the world's sixth largest according to \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  data - has been virtually flat since expanding 7.5 percent in 2010.\par \par \uc2 Economists expect the economy to grow only 1.5 percent this year, despite a series of rate cuts and tax breaks, and below the government's 2 percent forecast.\par \par \uc2 Mantega predicted growth would pick up again to around 4 percent to 4.5 percent on an annualized basis in 2013 in response to the lowered borrowing costs and stimulus measures the government has put in place.\par \par \uc2 Analysts are split over whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hold or cut rates next time it meets on Oct. 10, with the latest data showing a rise in inflation on higher food prices.\par \par \uc2 Mantega said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has room for further rate cuts.\par \par \uc2 (additional reporting by Alonso Soto in Brasilia; Editing by John Stonestreet and Phil Berlowitz)\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY-BRAZIL/ (UPDATE 3) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | CANT | G | RBN | J | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNA | UKI | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | Z | RNP | DNP | PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020120921e89l000uv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
