\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real slumps on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 , Mex peso dips\b0\par\par\uc2 524 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2012\par 20:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  cenbank sells reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps to weaken real\par \par \uc2 * Chilean markets closed for holiday, reopening on Thursday\par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds analyst comment)\par \par \uc2 By Natalia Cacioli\par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO, Sept 17 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real slumped nearly 1 percent on Monday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to offset possible dollar inflows stemming from last week's announcement of aggressive U.S. stimulus measures.\par \par \uc2 But Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  still appear poised to appreciate after the decision by the U.S. Federal Reserve to launch a third round of its bond-buying program. The move is expected to push yield-hungry investors into emerging markets, strengthen local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and potentially hurt the region's exporters.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, the government has so far been able to dodge the effects of the Fed's measures by stepping up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Mo nday sold reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps, derivative contracts that mimic the purchase of dollars in the futures market.\par \par \uc2 "What's important is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave a warning sign and markets are observing it," said Italo dos Santos, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  specialist with Icap brokerage in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 In less than one week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has sold about $5.7 billion worth of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps. The swaps were sold in four separate auctions, whenever the real strengthened toward the level of 2 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The latest of them drove the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  0.94 percent weaker to bid at 2.0296 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Under the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real has been trading within the narrow range of 2.0-2.1 units per dollar since early July.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico, the peso weakened 0.22 percent to 12.7675 per dollar as investors took a breather after driving the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to its strongest level in more than five months on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "Some low-level profit-taking is expected after the recent rally," Actinver analyst Jaime Ascencio wrote in a note, noting the cost of dollars in pesos had hit support at 12.73 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 The Mexican peso has led gains in Latin America, firming more than 3 percent this month.\par \par \uc2 Investors consider \uc2 Mexico's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the least likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. The bank is committed to a free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a stronger peso could also help policymakers fight a recent spike in inflation.\par \par \uc2 Chilean markets are closed for a national holiday and will reopen on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2051 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                             daily %  year-to-\par        