\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Opens Weaker as  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Paul Kiernan   \par \uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 September 2012\par 15:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real opened weaker Monday, as equities in Europe and stock-market futures in the U.S. traded lower and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market to discourage appreciation in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Around 8:55 a.m. EDT, the real was quoted at 2.0244 reais to the dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, compared with BRL2.0105 at Friday's close.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  extended its losses against the dollar when the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced, shortly after 8:30 a.m. EDT, that it would sell up to $3.5 billion in reverse-swap contracts Monday.\par \par \uc2 Reverse-swap auctions typically strengthen the U.S. dollar against the Brazilian real by offering investors the opportunity to exchange dollar-linked contracts for paper indexed to domestic interest rates.\par \par \uc2 But even before the auction was called, stock markets overseas suggested global investors were becoming cautious after a week full of encouraging headlines out of the U.S. and Europe.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve said last week it will launch a third round of so-called quantitative easing and buy $40 billion of mortgage-backed securities every month until the labor market improves. The rate-setting Federal Open Market Committee, or FOMC, also said it plans to keep its federal-funds rate near zero through at least mid-2015.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's bond purchases and low-interest rates have tended to flood financial markets with liquidity, pressuring assets like the Brazilian real to strengthen.\par \par \uc2 Brazilian authorities are loath to let that happen, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times with reverse-swap auctions to arrest the real's appreciation.\par \par \uc2 In addition, market participants are starting to question how much further the markets can gain before a correction comes.\par \par \uc2 "We are in an overshoot, we all know that we are in an overshoot, but the machine continues to roll on," Sebastien Galy, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2  in New York, said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Write to Paul Kiernan at paul.kiernan@dowjones.com [ 17-09-12 1309GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120917e89h000ob\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
