\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Stronger After Fed Announces QE3\b0\par\par\uc2 374 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2012\par 14:54\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Real strengthens to BRL2.0131 from BRL2.0192 at Thursday's close\par \par \uc2 --QE3 weakening the greenback against world \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expected to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent real from strengthening too much against the dollar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeffrey T. Lewis \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BRASILIA--The Brazilian real strengthened against the dollar Friday, a day after the U.S. Federal Reserve Bank announced a plan to inject more cash into the U.S. economy to boost employment.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real traded stronger at BRL2.0131 to the dollar, from Thursday's close of BRL2.0192 to the dollar, according to Tullet Prebon via FactSet.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Fed said Thursday it would buy $40 billion of mortgage-backed securities every month until the labor market improves. The rate-setting Federal Open Market Committee, or FOMC, also said it plans to keep its federal funds rate near zero though at least mid-2015.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The announcement cheered equity markets and weakened the dollar against many world \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will be ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to prevent the real from strengthening too far or too fast against the dollar should the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthen closer to the 2.01 level, said Luiz Carlos Baldan, director of the Fourtrade brokerage in Sao Paulo.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "They want the real between BRL2.0 and BRL2.05 to the dollar, so the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will step in" if necessary, he said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bad news from Europe returned markets' attention to the difficult situation in Spain, but various economic indicators coming from the U.S. Friday will have more of an effect on the real/dollar, Baldan added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Spanish banks borrowed a record amount of funds from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in August for the eleventh consecutive month, data released by the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shows Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  denied reports in the Dutch press Friday that it is in talks with the \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  about a bailout for Spain.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Citing unnamed sources involved in the negotiations, Dutch financial daily Het Financieele Dagblad said Friday that the ECB is negotiating informally with the IMF about a financial support package for Spain.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Jeffrey T. Lewis at jeffrey.lewis@dowjones.com [ 14-09-12 1254GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120914e89e000rd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
