\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: \uc2 JPMorgan\uc2  Sees More  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Ahead\b0\par\par\uc2 1,411 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2012\par 22:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 16:13 EDT - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government sees the weak exchange rate as insurance for the manufacturing sector, and is likely to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from appreciating vs the dollar until there's clearer evidence of a firm rebound in the economy, says \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 . Between Wednesday and Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $3.5 billion through reverse-swaps, moving its USD swap book from a $1.8 billion short position into a $1.7 billion long exposure, says \uc2 JP Morgan\uc2 . "We should expect daily auctions in the coming weeks every time USD/BRL threatens the 2.00 level, and spot \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should resume if inflows in the spot market improve." (matthew.cowley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 16:11 EDT - Some trackers of Shariah-compliant investment instruments, which comply with the moral and religious laws of Islam, have taken a hockey stick-like turn higher the last couple days. After doing nothing earlier this week, the S&P/TSX 60 Shariah Index started spiking up around noon yesterday and has gained 4% since. Same for the Russell-Jadwa Shariah Developed Index, which jumped 2% over the same time after being virtually flat over the previous three sessions. An anti-Muslim video appearing online sparked demonstrations this week across the Middle East, and led to assaults on US diplomatic compounds. (tomi.kilgore@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 15:53 EDT - As \uc2 Home Depot\uc2  (HD) pulls plug on 6-year struggle make big-box DIY centers work in China, analysts call the move a sound choice. \uc2 UBS\uc2  says it signals HD is willing to make right capital allocation choice "when circumstances are clear" but not a sign it would cringe from other international opportunities, like possibly Lat Am and "promising" China specialty concepts HD is experimenting with instead. \uc2 Barclays\uc2  says store closures highlight HD's focus on returns, noting company made a similar break from Chile and Argentina in 2000/2001 when management determined long-term profitable growth seemed dim. Shares up 1.8% at $59.33 after news earlier pushed stock to yet another 12-year high. (joan.solsman@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 15:52 EDT - Fossil (FOSL) looking to end the session strong, recently up 11% to $92.84, close to its high of the session. \uc2 Citigroup\uc2  feels the rise may be the result of "a decision [by] investors to rotate back into riskier higher-beta growth oriented names based on macroeconomic views such as a stabilizing S&P 500 and a more favorable credit environment." Firm does not believe that a "special situation or M&A event is imminent," such as the addition of a new licensed brand. Despite recent gains, FOSL still down 6.2% over the last year. (karen.talley@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 15:46 EDT - Friday's selloff wraps up a bruising week for Treasury bonds. The 10-year note's yield jumped by about 21bps for the week, the most on a weekly basis since March. The 10-year is recently 1 1/32 lower in price to yield 1.873%. The 30-year bond is hit even harder, with its yield up by 28bps for the week and recently yielding 3.093%. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 15:37 EDT - Egan-Jones downgrade of US reminds investors of a longer-term risk for bonds. Egan-Jones is a small rating firm compared to the big three -- \uc2 Moody's\uc2 , S&P and Fitch. The question is whether these big players will downgrade US in coming year. S&P already cut US to AA plus last year -- which ironically pushed investors into Treasury bonds and the dollar on safe-haven demand. \uc2 Moody's\uc2  has warned this week that it may strip US off the highest credit rating if lawmakers don't reach an agreement to fix the country's fiscal woes. If \uc2 Moody's\uc2  cuts US, Treasury bonds might get hit this time if the downgrade reduces investors' confidence to hold dollar-denominated assets. The potential pain will be on US consumers with higher interest rates. The 10-year note is recently 1 point lower in price to yield 1.868%. USD/JPY up more than 1.15% at 78.36. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 15:39 EDT - Given recent run-up in Valeant's (VRX) stock price following deal to acquire Medicis (MRX), \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  suggests investors take profits, downgrading stock to equal weight from overweight. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  believes market could be overestimating upside potential to VRX's $225M synergy target to boost earnings. Firm suggests "reimbursement pressure" on Solodyn acne drug, which MS estimates generates around 75% of MRX' EPS, "may constrain upside." VRX down 3.8% at $56.40 but prior to today, it gained 14% since news of the Medicis deal. (ben.dummett@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 15:28 EDT - Ratings firm Egan-Jones cut the sovereign debt rating of the United States to AA-minus from AA, citing the Fed's open-ended efforts to ease monetary policy. "The Fed's QE3 will stoke the stock market and commodity prices, but in our opinion will hurt the US economy and, by extension, credit quality," the firm said Friday. Egan-Jones said QE3 would reduce the value of the dollar, increase the cost of commodities, pressure business profitability and reduce customer purchasing power. "From 2006 to present, the US's debt-to-GDP rose from 66% to 104% and will probably rise to 110% a year from today under current circumstances," firm says, noting Spain has a debt to GDP of 68.5%. (patrick.mcgee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 15:24 EDT - Some momentum selling looks to be taking effect today ahead of Wednesday's F4Q report from \uc2 AutoZone\uc2  (AZO). Shares have continually been trending lower today, coming as \uc2 UBS\uc2  said before the bell in its earnings preview that "while AZO has been able to outpace in recent months, it has not been impervious to the industry slowdown. Thus, we think it is prudent to have tempered expectations for its 4Q release." Extending a decline from Thursday, AZO is down 4.1% at $354.88, approaching a 7-month low. (kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 15:21 EDT - The Fed's QE3 is ratcheting up inflation worries. The yield spread between a 10-year Treasury inflation-protected note and the benchmark 10-year Treasury security widened to 264 basis points Friday, highest since April 2011 and up sharply from around 240 basis points before the Fed announcement. That means investors expect a 2.64% inflation rate on average within the next decade. "It seems to me that the Fed's newest, boldest policy initiative risks the kind of deterioration in inflation expectations that, once unhinged, could be potentially incredible difficult to re-anchor, and would, in the process, wreak all manner of havoc in the Treasury market," says \uc2 Christopher Sullivan\uc2 , chief investment officer at the United Nations Federal Credit Union. (min.zeng@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 15:10 EDT - About 80% of trades on the New York Stock Exchange are attributable to subscribers of a package of proprietary market-data feeds the exchange sells, according to an SEC administrative order. The stat is a stark example of the extent to which sophisticated investors, typically relying on computer algorithms to automate and speed up trading, dominate market activity these days. It also shows how important such players are to the exchange's business core business processing transactions. NYSE parent NYSE Euronex (NYX) agreed to a $5M penalty to settle SEC charges its feeds gave certain customer an "improper head start." (matthew.jarzemsky@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 15:02 EDT - IPhone 5 preorder demand is such that \uc2 AT&T\uc2  (T) is now saying customers will have to wait 14-21 business days until shipment. Apple (AAPL) itself sold out of initial inventory in just an hour and \uc2 Verizon Wireless\uc2  is now showing delivery by Sept. 28, a full week after the phone hits shelves. Of course, previous experience shows that people may have a hard time getting the phone when it launches in stores, too. AAPL is up 1.6% at $694. (thomas.gryta@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par To contact the Market Talk Editors, \par Bradley Davis, 212 416-2654, bradley.davis@dowjones.com \par Kevin Kingsbury, 212 416-2354, kevin.kingsbury@dowjones.com \par John Shipman, 212 416-2181,john.shipman@dowjones.com \par Patrick Sullivan, 212 416-2326,Patrick.sullivan@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 09-14-12 1613ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4035   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020120914e89e000pk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
