\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE:  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Opens Weaker Amid  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Concerns\b0\par\par\uc2 793 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2012\par 15:17\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Concerns about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limit real's reaction to overseas moves\par \par \uc2 --German court ruling clears way for bond purchases by \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market also awaits news of fresh stimulus by U.S. Federal Reserve\par \par \uc2 --Brazilian real opens at BRL2.0177, weaker from Tuesday's close at BRL2.0168\par \par \uc2 (Updates with additional details, comment from trader)\par \par \uc2 By Jeff Fick\par \par \uc2 RIO DE JANEIRO--The Brazilian real traded weaker against the U.S. dollar at the open Wednesday as concerns about local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  offset positive news on Europe's ongoing debt crisis and expectations for fresh stimulus in the U.S.\par \par \uc2 The real failed to track gains by the euro, a key barometer for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and other global \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the U.S. dollar to open trading at BRL2.0177 to the greenback, according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet. That was weaker from Tuesday's close at BRL2.0168. The real later extended losses to trade at BRL2.0180 to the dollar as of 1300 GMT.\par \par \uc2 While global markets were enthused after Germany's highest court declined to block the country's ratification of the European Stability Mechanism, local traders were focused on possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . With the real churning steadily toward the BRL2.00 to the dollar mark, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fired a warning shot across trading desks during Tuesday's session. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  informally polled market participations about interest in a reverse-swap auction, one trader confirmed.\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  polled the market for interest, but didn't release the results," the Sao Paulo-based trader said. "It's not clear yet whether the bank will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or not. We're all waiting to find out."\par \par \uc2 The recent approach of the real toward the BRL2.00 to the dollar mark has in the past generated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Central bankers and government officials have kept the real trading in an informal band between BRL2.00 and BRL2.10 to the greenback in recent months via \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and tough talk from key government officials. The government appears comfortable with the real in this range because the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is weak enough to support local manufacturers and exporters without affecting inflation.\par \par \uc2 The auctions allow investors to swap \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions for government paper linked to interest rates. The interest rate paper is considered safer and less volatile. Typically, the auctions cause the dollar to strengthen against the Brazilian real by removing real exposure from the market. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has actively used the reverse-swaps in recent months to avoid a swift weakening in the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could hurt local businesses as the European crisis deepened.\par \par \uc2 On the flip side, the bank has also declined to roll over the swaps as overseas tensions eased in July and August. As the real strengthens toward the BRL2.00 mark ahead of the expiration of the swaps, the lack of a rollover then forces holders of the contracts to seek dollars in the spot market that causes the real to weaken back toward the middle of the informal BRL2.00-to-BRL2.10 trading band. The bank declined to roll over $4.1 billion in dollar-swap contracts that matured Sept. 3. An additional $1.8 billion will mature on Oct. 1, according to data on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Web site.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market now expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to likely act as overseas moves give investors a green light to seek higher returns. The German court ruling paves the way for the creation of a permanent bailout mechanism that will provide large-scale financial assistance for debt-saddled countries in the single-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bloc.\par \par \uc2 The move sent the euro to near a four-month high against the buck. In addition, yields on bonds issued by financially troubled euro-zone countries Italy and Spain tumbled. Now, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  will also be able to move forward with plans to buy sovereign debt of such countries on the secondary market.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders also expect global markets to get a fresh injection of liquidity this week from the U.S. Federal Reserve's meeting. The expectation is that a third round of asset purchases known as quantitative easing will be unveiled. Previous such measures by the Fed have caused the Brazilian real to strengthen against the dollar as investors seek higher rates of return.\par \par \uc2 The overseas news will likely add fuel to the risk-on sentiment, CitiFX said in a morning note. The firm expects the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , "holding [the Brazilian real] at 2.01."\par \par \uc2 -Write to Jeff Fick at Jeff.Fick@dowjones.com [ 12-09-12 1317GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120912e89c000rk\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
