\par\par \b \uc2 Brazil's Real Opens Weaker After Rate Cut; Eyes on Swaps, Fed, ECB\b0\par\par\uc2 By Matthew Cowley   \par \uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2012\par 15:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SAO PAULO--Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened slightly Thursday following a widely expected rate cut by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as investors turn to month-end swaps exipries and the possibility of more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks in Europe and the U.S.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Wednesday cut the country's key rate to 7.5%, from 8%, as expected, and gave a strong hint that the year-long easing cycle may come to an end, unless there's a turn for the worse in the domestic economy.\par \par \uc2 Any further moves would need to be conducted with "maximum parsimony," the bank said in a statement; furthermore, it dropped all mention of concerns about the deterioration in the global economy, which had been present in previous statements.\par \par \uc2 In the rates market, investors scaled back their bets on more interest rate cuts this year, and started putting more money on interest rate hikes in 2013.\par \par \uc2 The news has less direct impact on the Brazilian real given the targeted capital controls introduced by the government over the last year to prevent massive capital inflows.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the market was more focused on the month-end battle over the Ptax rate, which is used to settle monthly futures contracts. Some $4.1 billion in dollar-swap contracts sold in late June will mature Sept. 3, with the expiration of an additional $1.8 billion on Oct. 1, according to data on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's website.\par \par \uc2 The real weakened to BRL2.0532 per dollar, according to Tullett Prebon via Factset, from BRL2.0472 late Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is also wary of activity in the U.S., with Federal Reserve Chairman \uc2 Ben Bernanke\uc2  set to speak Friday at the \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City\uc2 's annual economic symposium. The market is looking for hints from Mr. Bernanke that the Fed may launch a new round of quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 In Europe, authorities are caught up in a row over the role of the ECB, and its ability to undertake massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in European sovereign bond markets. The market has been hoping that government debt purchases by the ECB, as indicated by its president, \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2 , would bring down Spanish and Italian debt yields to sustainable levels, but German officials have rebutted such a possibility.\par \par \uc2 According to Sidney Yoshiro at Citibank, the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may opt to wait until there are clearer signs from the U.S. and Europe before making a move. The real is currently in the mid-point of the range of BRL2.00 to BRL2.10 which the market perceives as comfortable for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "I think [the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ] will not roll the swaps, not only because of the level...but also because of potential easing coming out of the Fed and ECB. Instead of acting before Bernanke and Draghi, BCB could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at higher levels if necessary," Mr. Yoshiro said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Write to Matthew Cowley at matthew.cowley@dowjones.com [ 30-08-12 1336GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120830e88u000yv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
