\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real slips on cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 545 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2012\par 18:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Investors bet on likelihood of ECB bond-buying plan\par \par \uc2 * Chile's peso up 0.4 pct, Mexican peso off 0.3 pct\par \par \uc2 By Rachel Uranga\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY, Aug 21 (Reuters) - Brazil's real slipped on Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  moved to curb its rise against the dollar, while Chile's peso firmed on hopes the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will soon begin buying Spanish and Italian bonds.\par \par \uc2 Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had not waded into the market for several weeks, sold $350.2 million of reverse \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap contracts, which mimic the purchase of dollars in futures markets.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seen again signaling to markets that it wanted to keep the real from reaching a point where it would hurt local industries competing against cheaper imports.\par \par \uc2 "The market is being told 'don't move,'" said Pedro Tuesta, a Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with Washington-based 4Cast. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a lot of money. You don't defy a $350 billion \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and one that is very willing to use its power," he said referring to the bank's reserves.\par \par \uc2 The real weakened 0.05 percent to 2.0166 per dollar. The real has been mostly trading between 2 per dollar and 2.05 per dollar since the end of June on the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In addition to acting to protect local exporters, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policymakers have acted to strengthen the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if it weakens so much that it could raise import prices and stoke inflation.\par \par \uc2 The move to weaken the real comes after a spate of upbeat data showing that Brazil's economic doldrums may be hitting bottom. Last week the country reported the economy in June grew at its fastest pace in 15 months and retail sales clocked a surprising leap.\par \par \uc2 STIMULUS EXPECTATIONS WEIGH\par \par \uc2 Chile's peso gained 0.44 percent to 482.6000 as the price of copper, its top export, rose sharply on hopes for stimulus to the global economy from major central banks.\par \par \uc2 Copper for delivery in three months gained 1.72 percent in London, buoyed by both the outlook for Europe and expectations the United States and China may also provide more stimulus.\par \par \uc2 European central bankers on Monday sought to quash speculation that it will buy bonds of Spain and Italy to push down borrowing costs, but investors and traders contined to see hopes that the debt crisis is closer to resolution.\par \par \uc2 In Mexico, the optimism had a different affect on the peso with some traders selling off Latin America's most liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy up European assets, Tuesta added.\par \par \uc2 Mexico's peso slipped 0.33 percent to 13.1487 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2011 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2                              daily %  year-to-\par                                       change     ate %\par                             Latest              change\par Brazil real                   2.0166     -0.05     -7.34\par                                               \par Mexico peso                  13.1487     -