\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging-Market  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  and Debt Modestly Up\b0\par\par\uc2 By Prabha Natarajan   \par \uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2012\par 22:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and debt were firmer for most of the day, though there was some paring of gains toward the end of trading on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Investor confidence rallied on the hope of European leaders resolving the region's debt crisis next month. While there was no statement from the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on this, speculation that the ECB may consider capping the yields on weaker euro-zone nations has been making the rounds.\par \par \uc2 This helped push the euro higher against the dollar, and other higher-yielding assets rallied.\par \par \uc2 Emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also were buoyed by news that China is weighing stimulus measures to boost domestic consumption in a bid to boost its slowing economy and sliding exports.\par \par \uc2 "Its full steam ahead for hop-ium (or hope)," said Andrew Busch, global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and public policy strategist at BMO Capital Markets. "When the biggest unknown out there [Europe] stabilizes, then you are going to get people going back to higher yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 However, he expects the positive mood to last only until the meeting this weekend between German Chancellor \uc2 Angela Merkel\uc2  and Greek Prime Minister Antonis Samaras, when an extension of Greece's austerity target is likely to be on the agenda.\par \par \uc2 But such sentiment was absent Tuesday, when the South African rand and the Russian ruble were among the top gainers of the day to the dollar. The rand, however, is not expected to sustain its gains as the country's economic outlook remains bleak on falling demand for commodities, slowing growth and high unemployment. The rand is trading at ZAR8.2649 to the dollar, off from its 8.2124 earlier in the day, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 Just as market participants were waiting for the dollar to edge closer to 2 reais, in sync with a rally in all higher-yielding \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \uc2 Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced reverse swap auctions to buy dollars. That indicates the bank's comfortable range for the pair is BRL2-2.10, Citi analysts said. The move is the first dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since March 26. \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a bid to boost economic growth, has been weakening its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though some analysts have feared doing so would lead to higher inflation. The dollar is currently at BRL2.0178, slightly up from its previous close of BRL2.0173, according to CQG data.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Peru once again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to buy $40 million at an average of PEN2.6118 per dollar. The sol closed unchanged at PEN2.613 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 In Europe, most of the emerging-market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened across the board. The Romanian leu benefited from a move by its constitutional court to invalidate the referendum held to impeach its president. The leu has strengthened 0.38% to 4.477 to the euro on the news, and could rally further in the near term.\par \par \uc2 Emerging-market debt as measured by the Markit CDX.EM index was trading at four basis points firmer at 246, according to Markit data.\par \par \uc2 India's \uc2 Axis Bank Ltd\uc2 . (532215.BY) has priced a $250 million tap of its 5.125% coupon September 2017 dollar bond to yield 390 basis points over comparable Treasurys. The bonds were reoffered at $101.835 per $100 of face value, yielding 4.71%.\par \par \uc2 --Patrick McGee and Robert Kozak contributed to this article\par \par \uc2 Write to Prabha Natarajan at prabha.natarajan@dowjones.com [ 21-08-12 2042GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120821e88l000vp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
