\par\par \b \uc2 *DJ Brazil  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Director: No Signs Of Weakness In Job Market\b0\par\par\uc2 577 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 August 2012\par 17:05\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2012, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 3 Aug 2012 11:06 EDT *DJ  Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2   Director: Drought-Related Food Price Increase Is Temporary\par \par \uc2 3 Aug 2012 11:06 EDT *DJ  Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2   Director: Can't Say How Long Drought Effect Will Last\par \par \uc2 3 Aug 2012 11:22 EDT *DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2   Director: No Set Rules On When To \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  In \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market\par \par \uc2 3 Aug 2012 11:22 EDT *DJ  Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2   Director: Government Actions Should Improve Industry Competitiveness\par \par \uc2 3 Aug 2012 11:23 EDT *DJ  Brazil \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2   Director: Outlook Is For Slow World Economic Growth In Coming Years\par \par \uc2 3 Aug 2012 11:59 EDT DJ  \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  CB Director: No Set Rules on When to \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Jeffrey T. Lewis \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SALVADOR, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 --\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Brazil\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  doesn't have a set of rules its directors apply to decide when to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, bank director Carlos Hamilton Araujo said Friday.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There's no level that determines if the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  or not," he said at a press conference following a presentation on the regional economy. "We evaluate market conditions, and we make a decision to act or not."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been stepping into the market in recent months, mostly to keep the dollar from weakening too much against the real, but it has also acted to slow the dollar's strengthening.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earlier this week, the bank declined to roll over dollar swaps because market conditions didn't require it, Mr. Araujo said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Brazilian government has been concerned the real had strengthened too much and was hurting the country's exporters. Since the beginning of the year, the government has been taking measures to reduce costs for manufacturers.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Those measures, which include tax cuts and reducing red tape, will be the best way over the long run to improve the competitiveness of Brazilian industry, Mr. Araujo said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I don't think there's much doubt that some segments of the Brazilian economy suffer more than others from competition from the rest of the world," he explained. "Actions being taken by the government will improve efficiency in the medium- and long-term."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The government has also been acting to spur consumer demand to help boost domestic growth, as sluggish world economies have reduced demand abroad for Brazilian products.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The outlook is for global economic growth to remain slow in coming years, Mr. Araujo said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Slower economic growth has led to slower but still steady new job creation, and there are currently no signs of weakness in Brazil's job market, he added.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  expects the world economic situation to help bring the country's inflation rate close to the bank's annual target of 4.5% this year. The bank has a cushion of 2 percentage points in either direction, giving it a target range of 2.5% to 6.5%\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The annual rate in 2011 was 6.5%, and it had been declining since then until a recent inflation report showed a spike in food prices. The spike, which was caused by a drought affecting the southern part of the country, will be temporary because the drought will end, Mr. Araujo said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Jeffrey T. Lewis at Jeffrey.lewis@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribe to WSJ: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 August 03, 2012 11:59 ET (15:59 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020120803e883004mp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
