\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-EMERGING MARKETS-Latam  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  gains on ECB talk, US stimulus hopes\b0\par\par\uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juli 2012\par 23:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Refiles to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  central banker signals willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  real firms 0.34 pct, Mexico peso up 0.78 pct\par \par \uc2 By Rachel Uranga and Natalia Cacioli\par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY/SAO PAULO, July 25 (Reuters) - Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained on Wednesday, halting a three-day slide, as investors speculate that the U.S. Federal Reserve may soon deploy additional monetary stimulus and hopes rose Europe could stem the region's debt crisis.\par \par \uc2 The Brazilian real firmed by 0.34 percent and the Mexican peso strengthened 0.78 percent. Meanwhile, the Chilean peso was 0.65 percent higher.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymaker said on Wednesday he was open to the idea of giving Europe's new permanent rescue fund a banking license, which would enable it to borrow unlimited \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  money and boost its capacity to fight the crisis.\par \par \uc2 "Anything that increases the ability to purchase sovereign debt and extend the timeframe to which some euro zone countries may need to lower their debt levels and boost growth is seen as a positive development," said Clyde Wardle, a Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in New York. "But all of this is all based on comments rather than firm decisions."\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Brazil, Mexico and Chile all posted losses in the past three sessions as concerns were heightened that Spain could need a full-fledged bailout.\par \par \uc2 In the days ahead, Wardle said a jump in yields in Spain and Italy could weaken the Mexican peso, one of the most widely traded \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and highly sensitive to global economic sentiment.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, signs of a gloomy global economy limited gains in higher-risk assets. Weak readings on Britain's gross domestic product, falling U.S. new home sales and a German business sentiment survey all added to worries about the global economic outlook.\par \par \uc2 In Brazil, market players remained concerned the government would meddle in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if the real moves outside of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's comfort zone in the range between 2.00 and 2.10 per dollar.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Alexandre Tombini on Tuesday reiterated the bank is ready to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  into local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets when they are "not working properly."\par \par \uc2 Riskier assets, including emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , got a lift from a report in The Wall Street Journal on Tuesday saying the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  may be moving closer to more stimulus that would aid the economy.\par \par \uc2 The Fed's past bond buying programs have driven down yields on \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  debt and pushed investors to seek out higher yields in riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 "Expectations that the Fed may move up its third round of stimulus to August encouraged investors," said Luciano Rostagno, chief strategist at \uc2 WestLB\uc2  bank in Sao Paulo.\par \par \uc2 Latin American \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  prices at 2050 GMT:\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2          