\par\par \b \uc2 Brazilian Real Weakens as Spain, Greece Struggle\b0\par\par\uc2 502 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2012\par 22:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2012 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Brazil real weakens as European crisis intensifies\par \par \uc2 --\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders say\par \par \uc2 --Real exits active trading at BRL2.0465 to the dollar\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Brian Asher \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 RIO DE JANEIRO--The Brazilian real weakened against the dollar Tuesday, with investors seeking the safety of the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the euro-zone economic situation continued to deteriorate.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real exited active trading at BRL2.0465 to the dollar according to Tullett Prebon via FactSet, weaker than Monday's close at BRL2.0395 to the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The real tracked the euro's losses against the dollar as Spain's public finances appeared increasingly fragile and Greece seemed ever more likely to leave the euro zone.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yields on 10-year Spanish government bonds remained above 7.5% in Tuesday trading, a level that proved unsustainable for other euro-zone periphery economies such as Portugal and Greece. Yields shot up Monday on rumors that several of Spain's regional governments would seek central government financial assistance, adding to the chaos of an already-failing Spanish banking industry.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 French government officials called Tuesday for greater support to the Spanish government in the form of a larger bailout fund or a \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bond-buying program to lower Spanish borrowing costs, but a solution to the European crisis remained elusive.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 According to traders, the ongoing crisis will continue to pressure the real to weaken.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The instability generated by the crisis in Spain is leaving investors with a lot of risk aversion," said Reginaldo Galhardo, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  manager at Treviso brokerage in Sao Paulo. "Investors are looking for dollars not because of the fundamentals of the American economy but because there is a sense that the dollar is the only safe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  right now."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 With no end to the European crisis in sight, some traders are expecting \f28 \uc2 \f2 Brazil's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to begin playing a more active role in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has already announced new dollar-swap auctions for $4.570 billion on Aug. 1 and $6.250 billion on Sept. 2," said Joao Medeiros, a partner at Pioneer brokerage in Sao Paulo, "but those auctions will only allow investors to roll over their existing positions, so I think the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will announce more aggressive actions very soon."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Medeiros added with net capital outflows, a shrinking trade surplus, and a deteriorating external situation, the real will continue to depreciate without \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central-bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "I expect the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will begin selling dollars on the spot market," Mr. Medeiros said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Net dollar outflows from Brazil were $1.95 billion in the first 20 days of July.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, Brazil's year-to-date trade surplus through July 15 was $7.782 billion, just a little more than half the surplus of $14.830 billion for the same period of 2011.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Brian Asher at brian.asher@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subscribe to WSJ: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://online.wsj.com?mod=djnwires}}}\uc2 \f2  [ 24-07-12 2003GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1156 1843   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020120724e87o0015q\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (brazil near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000